</ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/taxtalentede/steuerberater-in-mindelheim-auf-wunsch-mit-partnerperspektive-gesucht-mindestens-90000eur-211038","tags":["Directors","Chief Executives"],"job_types":["Unbefristeter arbeitsvertrag"],"location":"Mindelheim","created_at":1793082642},{"slug":"senior-geo-manager-berlin-11690","company_name":"idealo internet GmbH","title":"(Senior) GEO Manager (m/w/d)","description":"<p>At idealo, we've built a strong SEO foundation. Now, we're looking to take the next step. As AI-powered search experiences such as ChatGPT, Google AI Overviews, Perplexity, and Gemini increasingly influence how people research products and make purchasing decisions, we want to ensure idealo becomes a trusted and frequently cited source within these new shopping journeys.</p><p>As our <strong>GEO Manager</strong>, you'll take ownership of developing Generative Engine Optimization (GEO) as an additional growth discipline alongside our established SEO activities. Combining your technical SEO expertise with hands-on experience in AI search optimization, you'll develop our GEO strategy, establish meaningful visibility monitoring, and drive experimentation to understand what makes content and data discoverable, relevant, and citable by generative AI systems.</p><p>You'll work closely with our SEO team and collaborate across Product, Engineering, Content, Brand, and Communications to turn emerging opportunities into scalable solutions.</p><p style=";"></p><h3>About your new role</h3><ul><li><p><strong>GEO Strategy &amp; Development:</strong> You develop and drive idealo's GEO strategy and experimentation roadmap, building on our existing SEO foundation. You identify opportunities across generative search platforms and AI-assisted shopping journeys, translating emerging developments into actionable initiatives aligned with our broader SEO and business objectives.</p></li><li><p><strong>AI Visibility &amp; Performance Monitoring:</strong> You establish and continuously improve a GEO monitoring framework covering platforms such as ChatGPT, Perplexity, Gemini, and Google AI Overviews. You define relevant KPIs, including mention and citation rates, share of voice, sentiment, and positioning within AI-generated answers, and develop dashboards that make performance and progress transparent to different stakeholders.</p></li><li><p><strong>Technical GEO Optimization:</strong> You leverage your technical SEO expertise to improve how generative AI systems discover, interpret, and reference idealo's content. This includes optimizing structured data (<a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="http://Schema.org">Schema.org</a>), semantic relationships, product and offer information, and identifying technical opportunities to strengthen our visibility and accessibility across AI-powered search experiences.</p></li><li><p><strong>Experimentation &amp; Competitive Analysis:</strong> You design, implement, and evaluate GEO experiments, analyze idealo's visibility against relevant competitors, and translate findings into concrete optimization measures. You continuously assess emerging GEO tools, methodologies, and platform capabilities to improve our approach.</p></li><li><p><strong>AI Shopping &amp; Content Optimization:</strong> You explore how idealo's product, pricing, and offer data can become a valuable information source for AI agents and agentic commerce. Together with Content Marketing, you assess existing content and develop answer-focused, well-structured formats that strengthen relevance, authority, and citation potential.</p></li><li><p><strong>Cross-functional Collaboration &amp; Knowledge Sharing:</strong> You connect technical SEO and GEO requirements with Product and Engineering initiatives and collaborate with Brand and Communications/PR on authority-building and digital PR opportunities. You actively share your expertise, communicate findings to stakeholders, and contribute insights from the evolving AI search landscape to idealo's long-term SEO strategy.</p></li></ul><br /><br /><h3 style=";"><strong>Skills &amp; Requirements</strong></h3><ul><li><p>3-5 years of hands-on SEO experience, with a clear focus on technical SEO. </p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Strong technical SEO fundamentals: site architecture, crawlability, indexing, Core Web Vitals, JavaScript SEO, and experience running full technical audits. </p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Practical understanding of how generative search systems retrieve, summarize, and cite content.</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Experience with data analysis, KPI definition, and translating data into recommendations. </p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Hands-on proficiency with core SEO tools (Google Search Console, GA4, Ahrefs or Semrush, Screaming Frog or similar crawler). </p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Familiarity with structured data, semantic models, and entity-based SEO. </p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Experience with GEO/AI visibility tools (e.g., Profound, AirOps, Rankscale, Peec AI, Otterly). </p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Strong AI mindset: willing to test new GEO tools and methods and share learnings with the team. </p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Excellent communication skills, able to present technical findings clearly to non-technical stakeholders across Engineering, Product, Content, Brand, and Communications/PR. </p></li><li><p>Experience in e-commerce, HTML, CSS, JavaScript, SQL or reporting automation with tools such as n8n are a plus.</p></li></ul><p style=";"></p><h3 style=";"><strong><span style="color: #121317">At idealo you can expect</span></strong></h3><ul><li><p><strong><span style="color: #121317">You want to further your education?</span></strong><span style="color: #121317"> We take your personal development goals seriously and, in addition to our idealo Learning Hub, eLearning offerings (e.g., Udemy), coaching &amp; mediation, we also offer you the opportunity to benefit individually from additional learning and development budget.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color: #121317">And what about the office? </span></strong><span style="color: #121317">Our office in the heart of Berlin offers free organic breakfast, excellent free lunch (vegan and vegetarian), as well as free coffee, lemonades and after-work beer, in addition to the "standard foosball". It also has a fabulous rooftop terrace with view of the whole of berlin where you can network with colleagues from our group of companies.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color: #121317">In need of additional support in any areas of your life?</span></strong><span style="color: #121317"> We offer free counseling and support in all areas of life (professional, private, family, health, etc.) in cooperation with the </span><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://mein.familienservice.de/en/"><span style="color: #121317">pme-Familienservice</span></a><span style="color: #121317">.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color: #121317">You want full flexibility on your way to work and beyond? </span></strong><span style="color: #121317">No problem with a job bike or Deutschlandticket - and it's environmentally friendly, too!</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color: #121317">Want to keep yourself fit?</span></strong><span style="color: #121317"> We offer many different fitness and sports options, such as an Urban Sports or Gympass membership, to suit your personal needs.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color: #121317">And what else is there?</span></strong><span style="color: #121317"> Of course, success must be celebrated! In addition to team events, you can also expect big company events and other moments of organized connection with others in the company and your team throughout the year!</span></p></li></ul><p><span style="color: #ffffff">#LI-MR1</span></p><p style=";"></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/idealo-internet-gmbh/senior-geo-manager-berlin-11690","tags":["Advertising","professional"],"job_types":["Full-time permanent","experienced"],"location":"Berlin","created_at":1793082010},{"slug":"account-director-enterprise-dc-berlin-berlin-frankfurt-am-main-hesse-hannover-lower-saxony-munchen-bavaria-354947","company_name":"Eunetworks","title":"Account Director Enterprise (DC)","description":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred locations are London, Berlin, Frankfurt, Munich and Hanover; with domestic and occasional international travel as required.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Driven by the rapid digital transformation of businesses across Europe, demand for high-capacity, reliable connectivity from Enterprise customers continues to grow. Thanks to our continued investment in the development of European fibre networks, euNetworks is a leader in Data Centre to Data Centre connectivity, supporting Hyperscale, Enterprise, Content and Wholesale customers across the region.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the Sales Director Data Centres you will play a key role in driving new business growth across the Enterprise market. You will do this by partnering, &#39;selling with&#39; with the sales teams of our DC customers to develop connectivity solutions for their DC tenants.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working in an experienced team, you will have the opportunity to develop and close large-scale European network opportunities (100G/400G) with Enterprise organisations that require high-performance connectivity across multiple locations. While you will also support the development of a small number of existing accounts, the primary focus of this role is building pipeline, acquiring new logos and expanding euNetworks’ presence within the Enterprise sector.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will have the support of our Sales Engineering team, with multiple engineers and additional account support available. You will also work closely with our Network Development, Digital Enablement and Product teams to shape solutions that meet customer needs and drive successful outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What will you be doing?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, target and win new Enterprise customers, building a strong pipeline of opportunities across the Europe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute new business sales strategies to expand euNetworks’ presence in the Enterprise market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build relationships with key decision-makers and stakeholders within prospective customer organisations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive opportunities from initial engagement through contract signature, meeting or exceeding sales and revenue targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a strong understanding of the Enterprise connectivity market, identifying trends, potential customers and new opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Network at industry events, customer meetings and campaigns to generate leads and strengthen euNetworks’ market presence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with Sales Engineering and Product teams to develop technically and commercially viable solutions for customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with commercial and finance teams to develop strong business cases and proposals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the development and growth of selected existing accounts, identifying opportunities for upselling and cross-selling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effectively manage sales activity and pipeline through Salesforce.com, ensuring accurate reporting and data integrity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What do we want from you?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant sales experience within Telecoms, Connectivity, Infrastructure or Technology markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong new business development experience, with a proven ability to generate pipeline and win new customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of meeting or exceeding sales targets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling connectivity, network infrastructure or data centre solutions to Enterprise customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An entrepreneurial mindset, with the drive to identify opportunities and develop new relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication, negotiation and relationship-building skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing complex sales cycles and multiple stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent organisational skills and attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A self-starter who is comfortable prospecting and building opportunities from scratch&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good understanding of the European Telecoms and Enterprise connectivity market&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If this position is of interest but you don’t think you meet all of the criteria listed, please consider applying still. euNetworks looks to recruit people with the right attitude, potential and ambition and for the right candidate, we will provide further training and support to enable you to develop in the role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What can we offer you?&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;At euNetworks we invest in our people by offering a range of benefits and development opportunities designed to support your professional growth and personal wellbeing. Employees have access to a comprehensive wellbeing programme that promotes mental health and also recognises the importance of work-life balance through initiatives such as a dedicated birthday day off and “give back” days to support volunteering activities. euNetworks’ bonus scheme is linked to both individual contribution and overall company performance with opportunity to overachieve in both areas. In addition, euNetworks operates a flexible hybrid working policy, enabling employees to balance in-office collaboration with remote work, fostering productivity, autonomy and a positive employee experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Family Friendly Policy delivers enhanced and inclusive parental benefits that can viewed &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1yM2VvLsByNiULKnRX9pIksCK0GI6FmO2/edit?usp=sharing&amp;amp;ouid=105588911760161167743&amp;amp;rtpof=true&amp;amp;sd=true&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Insurances, pensions, leave and additional enhancements are modelled to work with local country provisions, please email &lt;a ---------- for more details.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Diversity, Equity and Inclusion&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Our company values drive our behaviour and form the basis of how we operate our business. We work as a team promoting a culture of collaboration, trust and respect where every individual is heard.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are proud to be an equal opportunity employer and commit to providing each individual with the support, continued learning and the tools to achieve their goals and an environment in which they can thrive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We strive to make the hiring process equitable and accessible for all. Providing candidates with the opportunity to be their true selves and explore how you might thrive at euNetworks. We are a recognised Disability Confident employer and will make provisions where possible to support you through the interview process, if you require any reasonable accommodation through the selection process, please let your Talent Partner know.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What do we do?&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;euNetworks is a pan-European provider of bandwidth infrastructure services and a vital enabler of Cloud and AI adoption. We’re the leading connectivity partner for data centre companies and their customers in Europe, directly connecting over 600 data centres today. We own and operate 18 metropolitan city networks connected with a high capacity intercity backbone covering 53 cities in 17 countries. A leading provider of cloud connectivity, we&amp;nbsp;directly connect to all major cloud platforms.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/eunetworks/account-director-enterprise-dc-berlin-berlin-frankfurt-am-main-hesse-hannover-lower-saxony-munchen-bavaria-354947","tags":["Sales"],"job_types":[],"location":"Berlin, Berlin; Frankfurt am Main, Hesse; Hannover, Lower Saxony; München, Bavaria","created_at":1793073326},{"slug":"growth-manager-berlin-368876","company_name":"Buena","title":"Growth Manager (m/f/d)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Wir verwalten über 70.000 Einheiten in ganz Deutschland. Das ist nicht das Geschäft, das ist die Plattform. Darauf bauen wir neue Verticals auf: Versicherung, Energie, Finanzierung und Brokerage. Für Brokerage suchen wir jetzt die Person, die daraus ein echtes Geschäft macht.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Darum geht es</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Viele unserer Eigentümer wollen irgendwann verkaufen oder neu vermieten. Wir sitzen direkt an der Quelle und kennen Objekte, Eigentümer und Timing. Deine Aufgabe ist, daraus eine planbare Akquise-Maschine zu bauen: Du identifizierst die richtigen Eigentümer aus unserem Bestand, sprichst sie gezielt an und wandelst erstes Interesse in hochqualifizierte Leads für unsere Makler um.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Das ist keine Strategie-Rolle mit Folien und Roadmaps. Du baust selbst: Kampagnen, Outbound-Workflows, Automatisierungen, Funnels. Du weißt jede Woche, welche Zahl du bewegt hast. Du arbeitest direkt mit dem Leadership-Team, ohne Hierarchie-Ebenen dazwischen.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Was du machst</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Akquise-Engine aufbauen:</strong> Du analysierst unseren Bestand, findest Eigentümer mit Verkaufs- oder Vermietungsbedarf und baust Workflows für Datenanreicherung, Lead-Scoring und automatisierte Ansprache.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Marketing selbst umsetzen:</strong> Du baust und optimierst die Kanäle, die Leads bringen, von Outbound über Performance-Kampagnen bis zu In-App-Triggern im richtigen Moment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Funnel und Zahlen verantworten:</strong> Du definierst KPIs vom Lead bis zum Mandat, trackst Kosten pro Lead und Conversion und optimierst so lange, bis die Unit Economics stimmen.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Schnell testen: Daten-Trigger, Kanäle, Messaging und Lead-Magneten.</strong> Du hast eine klare Meinung, was du ausprobieren willst, und misst es sauber.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Was du mitbringst</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">3+ Jahre operative Erfahrung in Growth oder Performance Marketing, mit eigener Verantwortung für Leads, Conversion oder Umsatz.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Du hast Dinge von null aufgebaut, etwa als Gründer:in, als Geschäftsführer:in eines kleinen Unternehmens oder in einer frühen Startup-Phase. Das ist für uns ein starkes Signal.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on-Erfahrung mit datengetriebener Akquise: Outbound, Datenanreicherung, CRM und Automatisierung.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Marketing-Erfahrung mit Performance-Kanälen und Kampagnen ist ein klares Plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Erfahrung in Immobilien, PropTech oder Marktplätzen ist ein Plus, aber kein Muss.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Verhandlungssicheres Deutsch (mindestens C1). Du sprichst täglich mit Eigentümern und unseren Hausverwaltungen.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Du lebst in Berlin oder ziehst her und reist gern zu unseren Standorten in ganz Deutschland.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bitte nicht bewerben, wenn</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">du vor allem Strategie machen und die Umsetzung anderen überlassen willst,</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">du erst ein Team führen möchtest, bevor das Modell bewiesen ist,</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">du nicht bereit bist, in Berlin zu arbeiten.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Was wir bieten</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ein Vertical, das du von Anfang an prägst, mit 70.000 Einheiten als Basis und voller Rückendeckung vom Leadership-Team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ein Inside-Sales-Team, auf das du zugreifen kannst: Es übernimmt Anrufe und die Bearbeitung deiner Kampagnen, damit du dich auf den Aufbau der Akquise-Engine konzentrieren kannst.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Einen direkten Weg zur Verantwortung: Wenn Brokerage funktioniert, skalierst du es weiter.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Top-Vergütung inklusive virtueller Aktienoptionen und 500 € Wohnzuschuss pro Monat in der Nähe unseres Büros.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">110 € Lunch-Budget und 50 € Fitness-Zuschuss pro Monat, täglich Frühstück und Spezialitäten-Kaffee im Office.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">1.200 € Weiterbildungsbudget pro Jahr.</p></li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/buena/growth-manager-berlin-368876","tags":["Operations"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Berlin","created_at":1793072421},{"slug":"engineering-manager-control-low-level-software-munich-260369","company_name":"RobCo","title":"Engineering Manager – Control & Low-Level Software (m/f/d)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the Role at RobCo</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">RobCo is building the category of Autonomous Industrial Robotics and we're doing it fast. We believe that automating the ordinary frees humans to do the extraordinary, and we're building the end-to-end robotics infrastructure to make that possible - hardware, software, and AI in one stack that just works. </p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">At RobCo, we don’t just build robots, we are redefining the relationship between hardware and AI. Our end-to-end solutions seamlessly combine advanced, scalable industrial hardware with a central software suite powered by Physical AI to make manufacturing truly autonomous, efficient, and scalable. By delivering field-ready robotic solutions that just work, we empower industrial companies to automate without complexity and successfully solve the global labor shortage.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At RobCo, we automate the ordinary, so humans can do the extraordinary. To achieve this, we are looking for an ambitious <strong>Engineering Manager - Control &amp; Low-Level Software (m/f/d) </strong>to help us establish RobCo as a leading provider of automation solutions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">In this key role, you will lead the team behind how our robots move: RobControl, the real-time controller running on every RobCo robot, together with control unit software, robot modeling and hardware integration. One controller codebase drives our modular robots, OEM configurations and Alfie, our autonomous industrial robot, so your team's work reaches every robot in the field. Managing a team of control, embedded and software engineers, you will balance new capabilities for Alfie and our physical AI roadmap with the reliability factory customers expect on every shift.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Your Responsibilities</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own the hardware-software bridge:</strong> Lead the team developing our real-time controller, robot models, hardware interfacing via EtherCat, as well as core robot algorithms like motion generation and planning, calibration, etc., running on Linux-based Control Units.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Lead and Grow the Team:</strong> Act as a people-first leader for a mixed team of experienced engineers and early-career talent. Hire and coach, and balance roadmap work with field support through clear priorities and a fair on-call rotation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Drive Engineering Excellence:</strong> Set standards for code quality, hardware-in-the-loop and automated testing, and CI/CD, so that done means tested, released and running in the field. Improve observability so field issues can be diagnosed remotely and quickly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>One Platform for Every Robot:</strong> Keep one controller codebase for modular robots, OEM configurations and Alfie, extending it to new kinematic structures, more joints and multi-arm systems without forking it. Manage technical debt and architectural health as we scale.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Partner Across Teams:</strong> Work with Product Management, Hardware, Safety &amp; Compliance and Robot Intelligence to turn customer and autonomy needs into a clear roadmap, integrate RobControl with the safety controller, and support certification against ISO 10218 and ISO 13849.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Cross-Team Leadership:</strong> Mentor junior EMs and help evolve company-wide engineering best practices and software-first principles.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>We're looking for someone who has:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Completed a university degree in Robotics, Mechatronics, Computer Science, Electrical Engineering or a related field.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">3+ years of experience leading engineering teams that ship real-time or embedded software for robots, motion systems or other industrial machines.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep experience in robot control and motion is a big plus: kinematics and dynamics, trajectory generation, and position, velocity and torque control. Strong C++ and Python on real-time Linux, with hands-on EtherCAT and ROS 2 experience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven track record of driving an AI-first engineering culture and implementing agentic workflows that measurably accelerate team velocity and system efficiency.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Expert knowledge of modern SDLC practices for software that runs on hardware, including hardware-in-the-loop testing and staged releases, with a track record of improving release frequency and field stability.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working knowledge of functional safety for industrial robots (ISO 10218, ISO 13849) and experience working closely with safety and certification teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Culture-aligned mindset characterized by hardware empathy, a passion for software-defined hardware, and a strong culture of high ownership.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Very good English skills with the ability to navigate complex architectural discussions with Staff engineers while clearly communicating risks to stakeholders.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Why join RobCo?</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop modular, software-defined robotics solutions with us that set new standards in automation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help us build robots equipped with state-of-the-art AI that perceive their environment, analyze data, and make intelligent decisions in real time.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">As part of a very dynamic and fast-growing scale-up, you will take on responsibility from day one, drive your own projects, and see the direct impact of your work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flat hierarchies, open communication, and regular 360° feedback enable fast decisions and support your professional and personal development.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work out across Germany in over 7,200 studios with our subsidized Wellpass membership.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flexible working hours, a modern office, and—depending on the role—the option to work from home.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Regular team events—from relaxed beer &amp; pizza nights on the rooftop terrace to shared experiences on ski trips or at Oktoberfest.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About RobCo</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Founded in Munich in 2020, RobCo leads the transition toward fully Autonomous Industrial Robotics. Our mission is to deploy RobCo in every factory - solving the industrial labor shortage through end-to-end robotics that just works. Powered by Physical AI, our solutions combine a scalable modular hardware architecture with intelligent software that continuously learns and improves, requiring zero upfront investment through our Robotics-as-a-Service (RaaS) model.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We solve our customers' most pressing pain points - labor shortage, cost pressure, workplace safety, and national reshoring - across the full spectrum of Autonomous Industrial Robotics. In October 2026, RobCo reached unicorn status with a valuation exceeding one billion US dollars, with its valuation doubling in less than nine months. With $200M raised from investors including Sequoia, Lightspeed, Lingotto, Kindred, Cherry Ventures, and the European Tech Collective, 225+ people globally, and 3.5M+ operating hours in the field, we are deploying robots in factories across Europe and the United States - with our US operations headquartered in Austin, TX, and our Bay Area Lab in San Francisco.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Don’t meet every single requirement? If you’re excited about this role but your past experience doesn’t align perfectly with every qualification in the job description, we encourage you to apply anyway. You may be just the right candidate for this or other roles.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>At RobCo, applicants are selected regardless of ethnic origin, religion, gender, age, disability, or sexual orientation. All decisions throughout the recruitment process are based solely on applicants’ qualifications, skills, knowledge, and experience, as well as relevant business requirements.</em></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/robco/engineering-manager-control-low-level-software-munich-260369","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Munich","created_at":1793072415},{"slug":"leitung-physiotherapie-germany-migrane-und-kopfschmerzklinik-konigstein-26625","company_name":"PraxisEins","title":"Leitung Physiotherapie (m/w/d)","description":"<h1>Leitung Physiotherapie | Schmerztherapie (m/w/d)</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Mehr als ein Job. Eine Aufgabe mit Sinn – und mit Verantwortung.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Die Migräne- und Kopfschmerzklinik Königstein ist Deutschlands älteste spezialisierte Klinik für Migräne und Kopfschmerzen. Seit 1977 behandeln wir Patientinnen und Patienten interdisziplinär – als Akutklinik, zertifi