><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Unsere Mission</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Versorgung sichern - Qualitätsmedizin gewährleisten. Als PraxisEins wollen wir die Primärversorgung zukunftsfähig machen – mit digitaler Unterstützung, klaren Prozessen und einem Umfeld, in dem Ärztinnen und Ärzte Medizin wieder mit Freude ausüben können!<br /><em><br />PraxisEins ist ein Arbeitgeber, der Chancengleichheit fördert und Vielfalt schätzt. Wir freuen uns über alle Bewerbungen und bearbeiten diese völlig unabhängig von Geschlecht, Religionszugehörigkeit, Hautfarbe, Herkunft, sexueller Orientierung, Alter, Familienstand oder Behindertenstatus. Zur besseren Lesbarkeit wird in dieser Stellenanzeige das generische Maskulinum verwendet.</em></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/praxiseins/physiotherapeut-germany-migrane-und-kopfschmerzklinik-konigstein-155057","tags":["MKK"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Germany | Migräne- und Kopfschmerzklinik Königstein","created_at":1793072415},{"slug":"technical-product-manager-integrations-berlin-5388","company_name":"Prior Labs","title":"Technical Product Manager, Integrations","description":"<h2>Who we are</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Foundation models transformed text and images. Structured data - the largest and most consequential data format in the world - stayed untouched, until now. What LLMs did for language, we're doing for tables.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We pioneered tabular foundation models: TabPFN v2 was a <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="underline underline underline-offset-2 decoration-1 decoration-current/40 hover:decoration-current focus:decoration-current" href="https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-024-08328-6">Nature</a> cover story, has passed 3.5M+ downloads and 7,500+ GitHub stars, and runs in production from <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="underline underline underline-offset-2 decoration-1 decoration-current/40 hover:decoration-current focus:decoration-current" href="https://www.oxcan.org/news/prior-labs-and-oxford-cancer-analytics-partner-to-advance-liquid-biopsy-and-clinical-decision-making-in-lung-disease">detecting lung disease with Oxford Cancer Analytics</a> to <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="underline underline underline-offset-2 decoration-1 decoration-current/40 hover:decoration-current focus:decoration-current" href="https://siliconangle.com/2025/12/01/prior-labs-debuts-tabular-ai-foundation-model-scales-10-million-rows/">preventing train failures with Hitachi</a>. The hardest problems - millions of rows, real-time inference, entirely new modalities - are still open, and no one else is working on them at this level.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're a <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="underline underline underline-offset-2 decoration-1 decoration-current/40 hover:decoration-current focus:decoration-current" href="https://priorlabs.ai/about">small, highly selective team of 40+</a> with backgrounds from Google, DeepMind, Meta, Apple, Amazon, Jane Street, and CERN, led by <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="underline underline underline-offset-2 decoration-1 decoration-current/40 hover:decoration-current focus:decoration-current" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/frank-hutter-9190b24b/">Frank Hutter</a>, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="underline underline underline-offset-2 decoration-1 decoration-current/40 hover:decoration-current focus:decoration-current" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/noah-hollmann-668b9010b/">Noah Hollmann</a>, and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="underline underline underline-offset-2 decoration-1 decoration-current/40 hover:decoration-current focus:decoration-current" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/sauraj-g/">Sauraj Gambhir</a>, and advised by Bernhard Schölkopf and Turing Award winner Yann LeCun.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">In July 2026, less than 18 months after our €9M pre-seed, we <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="underline underline underline-offset-2 decoration-1 decoration-current/40 hover:decoration-current focus:decoration-current" href="https://priorlabs.ai/blog-posts/priorlabs-sap">joined SAP</a> as an independent frontier AI lab - same team, mission, and open-weights models, now backed by more than €1 billion over four years.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Most enterprises will never call our API directly. They will meet TabPFN inside the platforms they already run: SAP, AWS, Azure, Google Cloud, Databricks, or their own cloud. How well that works, how fast each release arrives there, and which platforms come next is the job of our Technical Product Manager for Integrations.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You take each model release from handover to live across every channel, working with the engineers who build the model and the partner teams who host it. Inside SAP you carry the product side of TabPFN across its platforms, from AI Core to SAP Analytics Cloud, and you help build the integration engineering team that will work with you. Several decisions are yours to bring to the table: which announced channels we build next, what a marketplace listing should cost, how support for all of this works.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You work directly with our product team, our engineers and the founders, and you report to the CTO. This suits someone who enjoys landing things on a date as much as deciding what to build, and who still likes being close to the code.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Take every model release live across SAP, the cloud marketplaces and customer environments, on a plan you build with product and engineering.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Be the technical counterpart for the partner teams that host TabPFN, from SAP's platform teams to the hyperscaler marketplaces.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Shape how TabPFN shows up inside SAP's stack and what the integration engineering team builds first.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bring the open channel decisions to the founders with a recommendation, and stay hands-on: listings, docs, smoke tests, a PR when it is faster than asking.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we're looking for</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Two or more years as product manager for a platform or integration surface: a product that ships into partners' platforms, or that other companies build on.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have shipped through gates you did not control, landed multi-team releases on dates, and made a large enterprise's process work for a small, fast team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You started as an engineer and never fully stopped: you read code, logs and scan reports without a translator.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are in Berlin or ready to relocate; Freiburg or New York can work.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What sets you apart</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have shipped into an SAP, Salesforce, Microsoft or Oracle ecosystem, or know the cloud marketplaces from the inside.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have deployed machine learning models and know what GPUs cost.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have worked at a startup, and you use AI tools to take real work off your plate.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Life at Prior Labs</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll work alongside researchers and builders who hold themselves to a very high bar - in the quality of their work and in how they work with each other. We move fast and still take the time to do things right.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our teams are based in Berlin, Freiburg, and New York - when you're working on something as hard as TabPFN, being in the same room matters. But great people come from everywhere, and in exceptional cases we're open to remote, which usually means frequent travel to one of our offices. Wherever you're based, the whole company comes together regularly for offsites to build and celebrate together.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Our Commitments</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">The best products and teams are built by people with a wide range of perspectives and backgrounds. We welcome applications from all identities and walks of life - especially if you've ever felt discouraged by "not checking every box" - and provide equal opportunities regardless of gender, sexual orientation, origin, disability, or any other trait that makes you who you are.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We care about how your data is handled - see our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://priorlabs.ai/recruiting-data-privacy">Recruiting Data Privacy</a> page</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/prior-labs/technical-product-manager-integrations-berlin-5388","tags":["Engineering & Science"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Berlin","created_at":1793072415},{"slug":"research-software-engineering-intern-munich-222265","company_name":"Quantumdiamonds","title":"Research Software Engineering Intern (f/m/d)","description":"<h1><strong>Description</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">QuantumDiamonds is building the world’s first commercial quantum sensing tools for chip failure analysis. As our Research Software Engineering Intern in Pre-Development, you bring our measurement software together. A measurement protocol is the recipe our Quantum Diamond Microscope (QDm) follows for one measurement: how laser, microwaves and camera are sequenced and timed, and how raw camera frames become a magnetic field image of a chip. Our engineers write new protocols whenever they test a new idea, and several backends for running them grew in parallel. You turn them into one shared Python framework that our engineers extend.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The challenge is a framework R&amp;D still uses long after your internship: flexible enough that a new protocol is a day’s work, automated enough that a measurement runs without someone watching it, and structured enough that the next engineer extends it without reading all of it. An experienced colleague from the team mentors you and sets the architecture; you make that trade-off real in code, working with Claude Code every day, as our engineers do.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a full-time internship for 6 months, during or after your studies, starting as soon as possible.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Who we are</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Founded in 2022 as a spin-off of TU Munich, QD leverages quantum sensors to rapidly capture three-dimensional current maps within multi-layer chips. Our strong, international team of over 70, including physicists, engineers, data scientists, and other experts, works side by side with major semiconductor manufacturers, supporting chip debugging and accelerating yield analysis. Backed by top-tier deep tech investors, semiconductor experts, and strategic public programs, we have ensured long-term stability, shifting from breakthrough to scale - and shaping the next chapter in chip testing.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Why join QuantumDiamonds?</strong></h1><h2><strong>Picture this:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Quantum sensors that see <em>inside</em> the most advanced chips on Earth, right where two frontier fields collide.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Nobel-Prize physics aimed at real customers with real problems, in production now, not someday.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Physicists, data scientists, and engineers building side by side, turning deep science into tools the industry actually runs on.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An international team that runs at hard problems for fun, where knowledge moves fast and so do you.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Still unsure about why joining us?</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll get to build a company together with a brilliant and welcoming team on a product that has never been done before.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">From Day 1, you'll own your own topics end to end and see the direct impact of your work on how the world sees QuantumDiamonds.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our technology is the cutting edge of tomorrow, starting today and not in 10 years.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll be part of a high-growth company backed by top-tier investors.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Let’s make the invisible visible!</strong></h2><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h1><strong>What will you do</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bring the measurement software of Pre-Development together into one shared Python framework, to a target architecture your mentor defines, and migrate the existing measurement protocols onto it.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keep the CI/CD pipeline on GitHub Actions healthy as the framework grows: tests, linting, packaging, releases.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Give first-pass reviews on pull requests from our engineers (tests, conventions, API conformance) before your mentor approves them.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help our engineers extend the stack: new measurement protocols become modules in the framework, and you validate the migrated ones on our QDm systems together with them.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Document the framework and hand it over so the team runs it on its own after your internship.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h1><strong>What is expected of you</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enrolled in or recently graduated from a degree program in computer science, software engineering, computational engineering, physics or electrical engineering with a strong software focus.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Available full time for 6 months, starting as soon as possible.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Python is your working language: you structure packages, write type hints and tests, and have refactored or consolidated code you did not write.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Git and CI are routine for you, and you know how to make hardware-dependent code testable: mocked instruments, recorded data and simulation, with runs on real hardware as a separate stage.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">AI coding agents are part of how you work, and you check their output the way you check your own.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You review code and take review well, you can agree on a common interface with engineers who each prefer their own solution, and you treat your colleagues as your users.</p