tes with buyers and customers.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As our business continues to expand across Europe and new products launch, this role sits at the strategic centre of our go-to-market motion. You'll shape how we position ourselves competitively, influence sales enablement, drive content strategy, and own competitive intelligence that informs both marketing and product decisions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a high-impact individual contributor role designed for someone who thrives on autonomy, strategic thinking, and executing with speed in a fast-growing environment.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What you will do</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define and continuously evolve the core positioning and value propositions of our cybersecurity offerings to ensure they resonate with technical and business audiences alike.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop comprehensive go-to-market strategies for new product launches and key service updates, in close partnership with Product, Sales, and Engineering teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Equip our sales and pre-sales teams with impactful enablement materials from pitch decks and training to battlecards, objection handling guides, and product demonstrations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and maintain a deep understanding of the competitive landscape to sharpen positioning, inform product roadmap influence, and support strategic decisions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define and oversee a content strategy that supports thought leadership, demand generation, and customer education across blogs, whitepapers, case studies, and decks.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as the connective tissue between Product, Engineering, Sales, and Marketing, ensuring alignment and clarity across functions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Apply deep knowledge of threats, technologies, and market trends to inform all aspects of messaging, positioning, and strategic planning.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>What you will need</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">7+ years of experience in Product Marketing, with proven expertise in the cybersecurity domain.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demonstrated ability to define product messaging, execute go-to-market strategies, and enable sales teams in complex B2B SaaS environments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong understanding of cybersecurity market dynamics, customer pain points, and competitive positioning. You can speak confidently about MDR, EDR, IR, and the threat landscape.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strategic and analytical mindset with a bias for action. Comfortable setting direction and executing on it with high agency.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven track record of leading, developing, and mentoring high-performing team members.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent English; German language (C2) is required</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Nice-to-have</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Startup or scale-up background at a high-growth company.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with positioning frameworks and go-to-market methodologies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Track record of successful product launches or market repositioning initiatives.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prior experience in vendor-led or partner-enabled go-to-market models.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>What we offer</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A meaningful mission: protect organizations across Europe from real-world cyber threats.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with top-tier professionals from national CERTs, intelligence agencies, and leading tech backgrounds.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Full strategic ownership of