, running systems reliably, and continuously improving how the team works. The ideal candidate has operated across both enterprise and scale-up environments and has a proven track record of driving growth within large, complex, regulated organisations.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Key Responsibilities</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead a team centred on a .NET back end, with front-end and machine learning components, helping engineers establish and validate their understanding of technical architecture and design end-user-centric systems and tools.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own predictable, high-velocity delivery — establishing healthy engineering practices, sensible estimation, and a smooth path from idea to production so the team ships consistently and sustainably.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive operational efficiency and reliability by automating processes — including monitoring and alerting — meeting SLAs/SLOs, reducing operational cost, and minimising toil to keep the team focused on high-value work rather t</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Continuously improve delivery and operational metrics (e.g. cycle time, deployment frequency, change failure rate, and incident response), using data to identify bottlenecks and raises the bar over time.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage team engineers across various seniority levels and disciplines while staying hands-on when needed. Cultivate an inclusive environment where every team member feels they belong, and mentors them in both their career development and interpersonal skills. Make a good team great, and keep it great..</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Oversee quarterly execution of roadmap delivery, ensuring the team stays focused on the right priorities and manages efficiently through dependencies and cross-functional hurdles.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate across Engineering, Product, and Operations to deliver solutions for merchant and internal dispute use cases.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and strengthen relationships with engineers, managers, and people leads across multiple teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Operating in a highly regulated financial space, ensure compliance with a range of control frameworks — from internal stakeholders such as InfoSec and Internal</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Audit, to external auditors, card schemes, and regulators.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Oversee the responsible use of machine learning and AI in dispute decisioning, leading the team to develop the infrastructure, tooling, and governance required to run models safely and at scale in production.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About You</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A resilient leader who has learned from setbacks and failures and consistently comes back stronger, keeping teams steady and delivering through periods of change and ambiguity.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You thrive on pace. You're energised by a high-growth environment, comfortable making decisions with imperfect information, and you keep the team moving and shipping when priorities shift under you.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A proven track record of driving predictable delivery and operational efficiency — improving throughput, reliability, and the team's cost of operation, and using metrics to back it up.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven experience building, growing, and sustaining high-performing engineering teams over time — not just standing them up.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience across both enterprise and scale-up environments, with a demonstrated track record of driving growth and delivery within large, complex, regulated organisations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A strong back-end engineering background, ideally in .NET / C#, leading teams building scalable, event-driven services and APIs. Comfortable also overseeing front-end and machine learning work, able to earn credibility and make sound trade-offs across disciplines even where you aren't the deepest expert.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Able to partner with Product Management to assess technical feasibility, provide capacity estimates, and balance new features against architectural health.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent time management and proactive problem-solving skills.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Technologies we work with</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Back end (primary): .NET / C#, REST APIs, event-driven and microservice architectures.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Front end: React, TypeScript.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Machine learning: Python, model training and serving, and the infrastructure to run models in production.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Data &amp; platform: SQL, plus experience designing batch and stream data-processing systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cloud &amp; tooling: AWS and/or GCP, Docker, Terraform, and observability tooling such as Datadog.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Knowledge of Kubernetes, Kafka, and CI/CD pipelines is highly beneficial.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Additional Information</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bring all of you to work</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We create the conditions for high performers to thrive, through real ownership, fewer blockers, and work that makes a difference from day one.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Here, you’ll move fast, take on meaningful challenges, and be recognized for the impact you deliver. It’s a place where ambition gets met with opportunity, and where your growth is in your hands.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We work as one team, and we back each other to succeed. So whatever your background or identity, if you’re ready to grow and make a difference, you’ll be right at home here.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">It’s important we set you up for success and make our process as accessible as possible. So let us know in your application, or tell your recruiter directly, if you need anything to make your experience or working environment more comfortable.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Life at </strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com"><strong>Checkout.com</strong></a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We understand that work is just one part of your life. Our hybrid working model offers flexibility, with three days per week in the office to support collaboration and connection.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Curious about what it’s like to be part of our team? Visit our<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.checkout.com/careers"> <u>Careers Page</u></a> to learn more about our culture, open roles, and what drives us.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For a closer look at daily life at <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com">Checkout.com</a>, follow us on <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/checkout/life/"><u>LinkedIn</u></a> and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.instagram.com/checkout_com/"><u>Instagram</u></a></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/checkoutcom/senior-engineering-manager-london-41819","tags":["All Departments"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1793018412},{"slug":"senior-analyst-stoke-on-trent-199608","company_name":"AMC Group","title":"Senior Analyst","description":"<h2>About AMC Group</h2><p>AMC  Group specialises in the recycling, trading, and upgrading of non-ferrous metals, while also driving innovation in electrification and decarbonisation processes within the industry. Headquartered in the UK, the business helps drive the metals industry forward through recycling, trading, and innovation, supporting the shift to electrification and a lower-carbon future.</p><p>Keeling & Walker Ltd. has 100 years of manufacturing, research and development expertise. The Company supplies high-performance metal oxides for variety of applications.</p><p>Main product groups are:</p><ul><li><p>Tin oxides – over 50 different grades</p></li><li><p>NIR absorbers – powders and nanodispersions for all your heat management needs</p></li><li><p>Laser marking materials – high contrast on variety of thermoplastics</p></li></ul><p>The role of Senior Analyst will be working for Keeling & Walker Ltd at their Quality Control Laboratory based at Stoke on Trent. </p><p>Main Responsibilities:</p><p>·         Improve performance and product analysis in the Laboratory,</p><p>·         Analyse production and finished goods samples according to SOPs</p><p>·         Document the results in Databases/ 1LIMS</p><p>·         Operate and maintain analytical equipment</p><p>·         Maintain and supervise 1LIMS System</p><p>·         Review quality records</p><p>·         Release materials for despatch</p><p>·         Develop or improve new analytical SOPs,  if needed in cooperation with the R&D Team</p><p>·         Cooperate with the Quality, Site and Production Manager</p><p>·         Develop robust methods for maintaining the quality of the analytical results</p><p>·         Introduce new equipment and methods </p><p>·         Automate routine tasks</p><p>·         BET Surface Area, Particle Size Analysis, Bulk and Tap Density, NIR Spectroscopy; Electrical Conductivity; Elemental Analysis by ICP,  XRF, XRD, DLS, Wet Chemistries</p><p>·         Support of QC and R&D team members</p><p>                                                                               </p><p>Requirements:</p><p>·         Experience in a QC laboratory, preferably experienced with different methods</p><p>·         Ability to work according to QC and ISO procedures</p><p>·         Hands on approach </p><p>·         Work under pressure</p><p>·         Microsoft office; ideally 1LIMS</p><p>·         Health & Safety procedures</p><p>·        Good communication skills </p><p> </p><p> </p><p> </p><p> </p><p> </p><p></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/amc-group/senior-analyst-stoke-on-trent-199608","tags":["Business Analyst"],"job_types":["Permanent employment contract (open-ended contract)","professional / experienced"],"location":"Stoke-on-Trent","created_at":1793012454},{"slug":"senior-process-production-engineer-stoke-on-trent-332490","company_name":"AMC Group","title":"Senior Process & Production Engineer","description":"<h2>Responsibilities:</h2><p>·         Set up and build an Engineering Department</p><p>·         Lead and Supervise a team (Process & Production Engineer,  Maintenance operator,  HPASA Engineer)</p><p>·         Digitalisation of the production and warehousing (Bar Code System)</p><p>·         Process Analysis and Improvements for existing production lines</p><p>·         Introduction of new products into production scale in cooperation with R&D</p><p>·         Introduction of new technologies on plant scale</p><p>·         Finding Engineering solutions for plant problems</p><p>·         Support & Backup for the Site Manager</p><p>·         Supervision/ Optimizing plant maintenance including buildings and general site</p><p>·         Supervision/ Optimization Site Security Systems (Cameras, lone worker system etc.)</p><p>·         Further development of statistical tools to control process and quality</p><p>·         Interaction with equipment suppliers, organisation and evaluation of trials</p><p>·         Interaction and cooperation with QC, R&D, EH&S, Sales Departments</p><p>·         Cooperation with the EH&S department to keep high levels of safety          </p><p>                                                     </p><p>Requirements:                                                 </p><p>Degree in Engineering, preferably Chemical Engineering</p><p>Good chemical knowledge</p><p>Experience in a production environment preferred</p><p>Experience with ATEX procedures preferred</p><p>Experience in Team Leadership on plant or division level</p><p>Good communication skills</p><p>Hands on mentality as it is a hands-on job</p><p>Creativity in finding engineering solutions</p><p>Computer literacy for Microsoft office software</p><p>High Awareness of Health & Safety procedures</p><p>Willingness to work flexible hours as required</p><p></p><p> </p><p><strong> </strong></p><p></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/amc-group/senior-process-production-engineer-stoke-on-trent-332490","tags":["Process Engineering"],"job_types":["Permanent employment contract (open-ended contract)","professional / experienced"],"location":"Stoke-on-Trent","created_at":1793010712},{"slug":"senior-digital-marketing-manager-107642","company_name":"Form3","title":"Senior Digital Marketing Manager","description":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THE ROLE 📝&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We’re looking for a Senior Digital Marketing Manager to lead Form3’s digital growth and demand generation strategy, helping drive pipeline growth and brand development across our priority markets.&amp;nbsp;Reporting to the Marketing Director, you’ll combine strategic ownership with execution across integrated campaigns, account-based marketing, digital acquisition and performance measurement. You’ll also identify practical ways to use AI, automation and marketing technology to improve targeting, personalisation, efficiency and campaign results. You’ll work closely with Sales, Customer Success, Product and the wider Marketing team, aligning marketing activity with commercial priorities and identifying opportunities within strategic accounts.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
