</div><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/ion-group/senior-business-analyst-contractor-london-203217","tags":["Product and Delivery"],"job_types":["Service Provider"],"location":"London","created_at":1792984070},{"slug":"chief-of-staff-london-453414","company_name":"Nous","title":"Chief of Staff","description":"<h2><strong>About Nous</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Nous is a household AI agent. It takes over the bills and admin people don't have time for and acts for them: switching energy, buying insurance, cancelling forgotten subscriptions, managing the family calendar. Nearly 250,000 UK households have signed up, and another joins every minute.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We think the real value of AI isn't writing amazing cover letters, it's doing useful things in the real world for real people. That's the hard part, and a brilliant product is only half of it. An energy switch takes weeks, so our agents run on long-running workflows, not a single chat turn. Cancelling a subscription means a browser agent handling the code Apple sends to your phone. Buying insurance meant getting our regulatory principal comfortable with an agent doing it end to end (a UK first), which comes down to knowing exactly when the LLM should hand over to rules because a mistake would cost someone real money.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're about 30 people running one agent across energy, broadband, mobile, insurance, mortgages and subscriptions (with more being added), each with its own suppliers, rules and ways of going wrong. With far more problems than people, a person or small team owns each one end to end, from spotting it in the data or a customer conversation to shipping the fix. And because the agent acts, you find out quickly whether the fix worked.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Everyone builds here: a product engineer launched our subscription cancellation product within a couple of months of joining, and a PM rebuilt our WhatsApp agent.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">And it's working. We're growing more than 20x year on year, with a market-leading NPS above +80, and we manage well over half a billion pounds of household spending. We've raised more than $30M from Heartcore, Mosaic and a who's who of entrepreneurs who founded Monzo, GoCardless, lastminute.com and Onfido. But the real draw is the team - ask anyone here why they joined and you'll get some version of "to do great work with really smart people".</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The goal is household life that's simpler, cheaper and fairer, and most of that is still to build.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>Why we're hiring</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Nous runs on small teams with real ownership and barely any middle management. That's a big part of how about 30 of us became one of the UK's fastest-growing startups. It also means the work of joining everything up has been spread across the founders and leads, squeezed in around their day jobs. Plans, OKRs, closing the hires that matter, the big company pushes: everyone does a bit of it and nobody owns it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Last week showed what happens when someone does. We ran "crunch week": five days where most of the company dropped its normal work to relaunch Nous as a household agent. Twelve workstreams, one owner each, a short daily sync and a pre-mortem. In a week we rebuilt onboarding and the website, shipped new agent capabilities, and got legal, security and comms ready for launch. As one of the team said afterwards, when we cluster around a problem for a bit, we do loads of work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We want that pace more of the time, without a founder having to drop everything to run it. So we're hiring a Chief of Staff.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>About the role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll work directly with Greg (our CEO) and the founding team, and own how Nous runs day to day: the pace, planning and OKRs, and the big company pushes, plus overseeing hiring and helping land the hires that matter most. You'll sit in the management meeting and get the full picture, including the things that aren't public yet. And you'll have the authority to change how we work: cancel or reshape meetings, and move people and cut scope during a big push.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You enjoy coordinating, but only because it gets things done faster. You'd rather get a decision made today than design a process for making decisions.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>What you'll actually do</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Set the pace. Spot what's stuck, work out why, and get it moving. Usually it's a decision nobody has made yet, so you get it made, or make it yourself.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own planning and OKRs. Quarterly OKRs, the weekly management meeting, planning and offsites. Squads run pretty autonomously; you make sure they're working to the same priorities. Each of these should take up less of everyone's time with you running it, not more.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the scorecard. Keep the numbers behind our OKRs current, and say each week what's off track and why. You pull the data yourself (SQL, our BI tool, a spreadsheet) rather than chasing people for updates.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run the big pushes. The next crunch week is yours: scope it with the leadership team, pick the owners, run it, and write up what we'd do differently next time.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Oversee hiring, and help close the hires that matter. Hiring managers run their own processes, and you won't be running ten of them. But you'll keep an eye on all of them, know where every search stands, and jump in where needed. Mostly that's closing the people we really want: working out what they care about and how to win them. Sometimes it's getting a recruiter excited about working with Nous, or unsticking a process that's gone quiet.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Represent Nous. You'll talk to recruiters and senior candidates from day one. Over time, and where it helps, you'll represent us to partners, suppliers and investors too.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Automate the boring bits. You'd rather build the Monday status digest with Claude than write it by hand every week. Anything you find yourself doing every week is a candidate for automating.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>What this role isn't</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An assistant. Diaries and inboxes are someone else's job.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A process role. If your first instinct is a new meeting, template or tracker, this probably won't suit you. With you here we should have fewer recurring meetings, not more.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A product role. Squads own what gets built, and strategy stays with the founders. You'll be in the room for both, and you make sure nobody's blocked.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A recruiter. You oversee hiring and step in where it matters; hiring managers still run their own processes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A dumping ground for jobs nobody else wants. You'll pick up odd jobs, as everyone here does, but the bulk of the role is above.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>What success looks like</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">In your first 90 days:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The company runs noticeably better: decisions get made faster and fewer things stall. Ask the leads and they'd say so.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Something that had been stuck for weeks has shipped because you got involved.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've helped close at least one hire we really wanted.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Next quarter's OKRs are set, and the scorecard is current every week.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">At least one piece of weekly coordination (the OKR update, the status round-up) runs as an AI workflow you built, and nobody does it by hand any more.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We have fewer recurring meetings than when you joined.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">After a year:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've led two or three company-wide pushes that shipped what they set out to.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The senior hires you helped close have said yes and are doing well.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Planning, OKRs and the weekly meetings run fine for a month without you.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Most of the routine coordination runs on workflows and tools you built, not on meetings.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>About you</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've got 4–7 years behind you (perhaps a little more if you've switched careers), probably a mix of a fast-growing startup and somewhere that taught you structure: consulting, BizOps or strategy and ops at a scale-up, a founder's office, or product work where you ran launches across teams. Maybe you've founded something.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You coordinate because you're impatient. You notice the thing that's been stuck for a week, and you're the one who unsticks it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're persuasive. You can work out what a candidate is really optimising for and how to close them, get a busy recruiter excited about Nous, and hold your own with senior people outside the company.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're comfortable with numbers. You can build a quick model, write a bit of SQL or find the right dashboard, and tell a real trend from noise.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">AI tooling is already how you work. Claude, Claude Code or similar is where you get things done, not something you tried once.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You write clearly and quickly. Most of this job happens in writing: kick-off notes, weekly updates, closing emails.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You tell people the truth, founders included, and you keep confidences. You'll see salaries, plans and people issues before anyone else does.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You listen and you care, but you don't do politics. This role has more connective tissue with others than anyone else in the business, so by playing it straight and being an honest broker, you are also establishing an important norm.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Low ego. Some of the job is unglamorous and you do it anyway.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bonus points:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've closed hard candidates, or worked in recruiting, talent or BD.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've run a company planning cycle, an offsite or a launch end to end.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've worked somewhere regulated (energy, fintech, insurance).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've automated a chunk of your own job and have something to show for it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are commercially astute or professionally experienced in a deep domain like law or accounting.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>How you will grow</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">This might not be a forever role, and that's fine. You'll see more of how a fast-growing company works than almost anyone else here, which tends to open doors: running a new category as we expand, leading a function, or a commercial or operations role. Or the role grows with the company. Either way, we'll talk about it properly once you've been here a year.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>Remuneration and benefits</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Compelling packages, including share options with life-changing upside. We've raised enough money to pay real salaries. We're building something great together and we all share in the upside. If we win, we win together.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">An environment where you can do your best work:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">🏢 A great office set up for lots of collaborative working. We already need more whiteboards</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">💻 The equipment / setup / training you need to do your best work (and of course, AI subscriptions, including Claude Code Max tier)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">🤝 A high-context environment with lots of exposure to the big decisions - be in the room when it happens (literally)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">🏡 Flexibility around remote work. If you sometimes just need to get your head down, that's fine</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">☕ Very good coffee</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">🍽️ A well-stocked kitchen (featuring a wildly popular toastie maker) so you can always make yourself a breakfast or light lunch on the house</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">🎉 Informal social every week, something bigger every month, plus a set-piece event in the summer and again at Christmas - we're not robots!</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">✈ 33 days paid holidays (including bank holidays)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">💊 Health and dental cash plans, including an employee assistance programme</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">🚴 Travel benefits, including the cycle-to-work scheme and season ticket loans</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Nous has an office-first culture. That means we encourage in-person working, and most people do work from the office in Farringdon most of the time. We do a lot of brainstorming, problem-solving and interaction within the team and presence makes this more effective. It also helps ensure people have good peripheral awareness and high context. But we are pragmatic not doctrinal about this, and recognise that, sometimes, certain types of work can be better done remotely. Most team members spend 3-4 days a week in the office on average. This role may naturally involve even more presence than that.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>The environment</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Most importantly, this is a high-performance, high-agency and high-trust technical environment. Nous is intentionally lean and AI-native, not just in its product but as a company. Everyone is expected to use AI to its full potential, whether that's debugging a system, streamlining a workflow or improving how customers are served. Rather than building layers of middle management, we hire smart, high-agency people and give them real ownership.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're dedicated to fostering an inclusive and equitable workplace, and we actively welcome applications from individuals of all backgrounds. Every candidate is thoughtfully considered, without regard to race, religion, gender expression, disability or sexual orientation.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you don't tick every box but think you'd be great at this, get in touch anyway.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/nous/chief-of-staff-london-453414","tags":["Central (General & Administrative)"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Nous HQ","created_at":1792975228},{"slug":"product-manager-london-311824","company_name":"Nous","title":"Product Manager","description":"<h2><strong>About Nous</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Nous is a household AI agent. It takes over the bills and admin people don't have time for and acts for them: switching energy, buying insurance, cancelling forgotten subscriptions, managing the family calendar. Nearly 250,000 UK households have signed up, and another joins every minute.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We think the real value of AI isn't writing amazing cover letters, it's doing useful things in the real world for real people. That's the hard part, and a brilliant product is only half of it. An energy switch takes weeks, so our agents run on long-running workflows, not a single chat turn. Cancelling a subscription means a browser agent handling the code Apple sends to your phone. Buying insurance meant getting our regulatory principal comfortable with an agent doing it end to end (a UK first), which comes down to knowing exactly when the LLM should hand over to rules because a mistake would cost someone real money.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're about 30 people running one agent across energy, broadband, mobile, insurance, mortgages and subscriptions (with more being added), each with its own suppliers, rules and ways of going wrong. With far more problems than people, a person or small team owns each one end to end, from spotting it in the data or a customer conversation to shipping the fix. And because the agent acts, you find out quickly whether the fix worked.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Everyone builds here: a product engineer launched our subscription cancellation product within a couple of months of joining, and a PM rebuilt our WhatsApp agent.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">And it's working. We're growing more than 20x year on year, with a market-leading NPS above +80, and we manage well over half a billion pounds of household spending. We've raised more than $30M from Heartcore, Mosaic and a who's who of entrepreneurs who founded Monzo, GoCardless, lastminute.com and Onfido. But the real draw is the team - ask anyone here why they joined and you'll get some version of "to do great work with really smart people".</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The goal is household life that's simpler, cheaper and fairer, and most of that is still to build.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>How we build (worth reading before the role)</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">How products get built is changing fast. With AI tooling, a PM can prototype, dig into production data and commit production code to get a change live all in an afternoon. An engineer can own a product area end to end and decide what to build next.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're leaning into that. Our PMs lean into code and our engineers run products: one of our engineers owns the car insurance targets. We care about whatever gets the job done most effectively, regardless of once upon a time whose job it was meant to be.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're moving fast and adapting as we go, and we don't have all the answers yet. What should a squad look like when everyone can build? Where does process still help, and where does it just slow you down? What's a PM for when an engineer can run the experiment themselves? We're working it out, and we want someone who is excited to be part of helping figure it out.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>About the role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">So where does a PM fit? A lot of our work still suits squads: clear targets, a few service lines and a team of engineers. Those squads need product managers to run them. All our roles in product overlap, but this one is centred on product management. If you’d rather spend all your time building, have a look at our Product Builder role.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll take a squad responsible for a key section of our product and service lines and grow them: expand what they cover, understand the levers that drive their performance (automation, new suppliers, what we recommend to members) and increase their commercial value.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Being a Product Manager at Nous is one of the hardest roles we have. The product is complex and we move fast, so you need to be able to hold a lot of context. You'll switch between very different things all day: thinking about OKRs and the plan for the next couple of weeks one moment, getting a PR into production the next, while helping unblock an engineer.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">That's also what makes it exciting.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You bring order to fast-moving work, get some sequencing in place so people aren’t each figuring it out on their own, evaluate what’s being shipped, own the reporting and keep the squad’s energy up. You won’t hesitate to make changes yourself, but you won’t be just another builder in the squad either: when you’re heads-down building, you can’t unblock anyone or bring the team together.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Growing a service line here means working across the boundary between product and commercial, so we’re particularly interested in PMs who’ve had real exposure to the commercial side of a business.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our agent acts in the real world a lot, so saving someone money takes more than great product execution. We also need access to the best tariffs and suppliers, and we have to understand the regulation we operate in. And because Nous is an agent, your nice neat Amplitude funnels don't work: every user's journey can be totally different. So we're after PMs who are excited by everything it takes to make an agentic product work for real households, including the bits that wouldn't traditionally count as "product".</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Worth being upfront: we can't tell you yet which service lines you'd own. It depends on the Venn diagram of your particular skill set and the problems we need to solve at the point you join.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>What matters most</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We need all of these at once:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sharp. You pick things up quickly and enjoy hard problems. Given a messy one, you can lay out what you know and what you'd check first, then change your mind as new data turns up.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Adaptable. We’re working a lot of this out as we go, so the role and the squad will change, probably more than once. You enjoy that. You pick up whatever’s needed, PM work or not, and you work in the open: sharing rough thinking early and changing course when someone has a better idea.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Delivery. You bring order to a fast-moving squad: clear priorities, sensible sequencing, people unblocked quickly, and an honest look at whether what shipped actually worked.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Product craft. You find the real problem behind a request and make the trade-offs explicit. You care about the details of what our users actually see.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Commercial and analytical. You know what your area made last month, what moved it and what you'd do next, and you answer most of your own questions with data. You think in conversion, margin and lifetime value as readily as in features.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Energy. You've probably worked at a startup. You move fast, you're happy doing the unglamorous work yourself, and you'd rather ship this week's version than polish next quarter's.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">And everyone builds here, PMs included. You'll use AI tooling (Claude Code or whatever gets it done) to prototype, dig into data and ship changes yourself. You don't need to be an engineer, but you shouldn't be scared of code.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>What you'll actually do</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Grow your service lines. Understand what really drives their performance, be able to measure it, and lead the squad to deliver it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Set the squad's OKRs and roadmap, get the sequencing in place, and drive fast, efficient execution.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Evaluate what’s being shipped, and own the reporting: make sure the reports and the data behind them make sense.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work across product and commercial: the suppliers and tariffs we can offer, the regulation we work within, and what that means for what gets built.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run experiments, and unblock yourself on the analysis without always needing an analyst.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Get close to members and ops. Read the conversations, sit with the people handling the edge cases, and fix the parts of the journey where people drop out or get stuck.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>About you</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll likely thrive here if:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've been a PM for a few years, ideally at a startup, and you've owned something with a number attached: revenue, conversion, retention.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've worked on the commercial side as well as the product side: a P&amp;L, a supplier or partner relationship, pricing, or a whole service line.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're comfortable enough with data and code to unblock yourself.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Nice-to-haves:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You were a software engineer before you moved into product.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've worked on a transactional or regulated product: insurance, fintech, energy, marketplaces.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've built and shipped your own thing: a startup, a side project, an internal tool that took off.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">This probably isn't for you if your PM experience is mostly roadmaps and stakeholder management at a big company, with no number you owned.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>How we work</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We keep the middle thin, on purpose. There's barely any middle management, which means fewer bottlenecks and room for exceptional people to have real impact without first being promoted into managing others. It's a real bet, not a free lunch. Instead of a manager buffer, you get lots of context and colleagues who help because they're invested, not because an org chart says so. If you need a clear remit handed down before you can move, this probably won't suit you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your first 90 days are built around getting you to real ownership safely: pairing when you want it, lots of context, and people who want you to ship. We celebrate the person who built the unglamorous version this week, not whoever thought of it first.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're office-first, near Farringdon. We do a lot of our best thinking together and being in the same room helps, though we're pragmatic about heads-down work when you need it.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>Remuneration and benefits</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Compelling package including share options with life-changing upside. We've raised enough to pay real salaries, and we all share in the upside. If we win, we win together.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">🏢 A great office set up for collaborative work (we already need more whiteboards)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">💻 The equipment, setup and training you need to do your best work</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">🤝 A high-context environment with real exposure to the big decisions, in the room when it happens</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">☕ Very good coffee</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">🍽️ A well-stocked kitchen (featuring a wildly popular toastie maker)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">🎉 Informal social every week, something bigger every month</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">✈️ 33 days paid holiday (including bank holidays)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">💊 Health and dental cash plans, including an employee assistance programme</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">🚴 Travel benefits, including the cycle-to-work scheme and season ticket loans</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you don't tick every box but think you'd be great at this, get in touch anyway.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/nous/product-manager-london-311824","tags":["Product"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Nous HQ","created_at":1792975228},{"slug":"value-engineer-london-131809","company_name":"Legora","title":"Value Engineer","description":"<h2>About Us</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Legora is redefining how legal work gets done. Not built for lawyers, built with them. We work alongside the world’s best legal teams, who expect excellence, precision, and speed, and we hold ourselves to the same bar.<br /><br />Our AI-native workspace lets legal professionals move faster, think more clearly, and operate with sharper precision. By analysing thousands of documents in minutes and powering end-to-end workflows, we cut through complexity, teams can focus on what matters: judgment, strategy, and outcomes.<br /><br />2,100+ customers across 80+ countries trust us, including Cleary Gottlieb, Goodwin, Linklaters, White &amp; Case, Dentons, and Barclays. We’ve scaled to<strong> $200M+ in ARR</strong>, with teams across Europe, North America and APAC, and continue to expand through acquisitions including Qura, Walter AI, Graceview, Cadastral, and Wexler.<br /><br />We partner with world-class performers: including Aaron Judge and the New York Yankees, Ludvig Åberg (and his caddie), and campaigns featuring Jude Law.<br /><br />Joining Legora means three things.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We <strong>lean in: </strong>ownership over titles, outcomes over intentions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We <strong>fight for excellence:</strong> high standards, direct, ego-free feedback.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We<strong> grow together:</strong> as a team and with our customers.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mission before ego. Everyone contributes. No one coasts.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you’re driven by impact, pace, and raising the bar. This is the place.</p><h2><strong>The Role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for a <strong>Value Engineer</strong> to join Legora in the UK, sitting at the intersection of Sales, Product, and Customer Success.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will partner directly with prospects and customers to quantify, articulate, and demonstrate the business impact of Legora. Working alongside Account Executives and Sales/Legal Engineers, you will translate complex legal workflows and quantitative findings into clear, executive-ready value narratives.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As the first Value Engineer in the region, you will play a key role in establishing how we lead value-based customer conversations and enable our go-to-market teams. You will work directly with General Counsel, CFOs, and other C-level stakeholders.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Accelerate strategic deals by partnering with Account Executives and Sales/Legal Engineers to build compelling, executive-ready value narratives.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Translate customer workflows, operational challenges, and quantitative results into clear financial and business impact.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead value-focused conversations with General Counsel, CFOs, and other senior executives.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop and deliver value enablement training for sales and go-to-market teams across the region.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create practical frameworks, tools, and assets that help teams communicate Legora’s value consistently.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate across Sales, Product, and Customer Success to share customer feedback, feature requests, and industry trends relating to value and ROI.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support customer adoption and expansion by helping customers understand and measure the impact of Legora.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>What You’ll Bring</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience translating quantitative results and complex workflows into clear, actionable business insights.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ability to build credible and compelling value narratives for customers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience engaging directly with senior executives in a clear, confident, and concise way.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong communication skills, with the ability to simplify complex ideas for different audiences.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ability to prioritise effectively and deliver high-quality outputs quickly without over-engineering.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A proactive, hands-on approach and enthusiasm for being the first person in this role within the region.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Preferred Qualifications</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluency in French or German.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An interest in teaching, coaching, and enabling sales teams.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Location</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">London preferred, with Stockholm also considered.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Legora is an Equal Opportunity Employer</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Legora, we believe great teams are built on diversity of thought and experience. We’re proud to be an equal opportunity employer and committed to creating an inclusive, high-performance culture where everyone can do their best work. We welcome people of all backgrounds and don’t discriminate based on race, color, religion, national origin, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, age, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/legora/value-engineer-london-131809","tags":["Go To Market (GTM)"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1792975226},{"slug":"remote-technical-support-engineer-22092","company_name":"Plaid","title":"Technical Support Engineer","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">We believe that the way people interact with their finances will drastically improve in the next few years. We’re dedicated to empowering this transformation by building the tools and experiences that thousands of developers use to create their own products. Plaid powers the tools millions of people rely on to live a healthier financial life. We work with thousands of companies like Venmo, SoFi, several of the Fortune 500, and many of the largest banks to make it easy for people to connect their financial accounts to the apps and services they want to use. Plaid’s network covers 12,000 financial institutions across the US, Canada, UK and Europe. Founded in 2013, the company is headquartered in San Francisco with offices in New York, Seattle, Washington D.C., Raleigh, London, and Amsterdam.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The Customer Support Team helps customers  improve their experience using Plaid Products through collaborative issue resolution.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Customer-obsessed</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Problem Solvers</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Technically Savvy</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborative</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Today, Plaid Support ensures our customers' applications can help their consumers live their best financial lives by ensuring our products continue to operate as expected. We investigate the root cause of integration issues, quantify their scope and impact, and when we can’t fix them ourselves, we work with our Go-to-Market, Engineering, and Product teams to reach a solution.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As we continue to grow, we’re looking for Technical Support Engineers (TSEs) to join the team to help us balance the needs of customers, users and internal stakeholders, while navigating critical technical issues. In this role, you will manage issues from their first symptom to their eventual resolution, communicating with our customers and internal stakeholders throughout the process. People who succeed in this role tend to be empathetic, collaborative, technically minded, and most importantly - customer-centric. They have an interest in learning more about financial services, and are excited to help customers resolve complex issues. TSEs become embedded within engineering teams at Plaid, and we have a high technical bar to ensure that we all speak the same language. Our Support team sets aggressive goals to meet the standards our customers expect, and we collaborate cross-functionally with our Engineering, Product, Financial Access, and Go-to-Market teams in order to achieve these goals.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Responsibilities: </p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Interface with customers via Zendesk tickets</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Troubleshoot customer issues using internal tools and documentation and escalate to Engineering or Partnership teams for resolution</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work on projects with other TSE’s to improve internal and external processes</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Respond to 10+ customer tickets per day, meeting quality standards</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute to brainstorming and project execution (tooling, documentation, process improvements)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Assist GTM teams with customer escalations</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate with EPD teams on issue resolution</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Qualifications: </p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">2+ years of experience in a customer-facing role</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">6+ months of experience working with REST APIs, SQL, CSS, HTML and a coding language (Javascript or Python)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Knowledge of ticketing systems and tools (e.g. Zendesk, Linear), and data visualizations (e.g. Databricks)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Preferred: 6+ months of experience supporting technical projects and/or process improvement</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Genuine interest and passion for Support</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Commitment to 