sues across our growing Stablecoin operations. You'll also be involved in funding forecasts to ensure that our partners are well funded at all times.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll work directly with our trading team as well as collaborating with the wider team that spans the globe ( London, Abidjan, Lagos, Nairobi, Paris and New York, to name a few places), ensuring that Taptap Send is effectively supported in its growth and customer ambitions! There is plenty of room for professional progression and personal growth within our friendly and ever-growing Taptap community.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2></h2><h2><strong>Responsibilities</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proactively managing treasury operations, initially for stablecoins, to ensure our accounts are funded and payments can be processed seamlessly</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working closely with partners to ensure that funding timelines are being delivered on time</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Troubleshooting to find root causes of payment issues and working with internal and external partners to resolve</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Assisting with onboarding new banks and trading partners for stablecoin, working closely with our business development team</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Providing out-of-hours coverage when required</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Requirements</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have at least 1 years’ experience, ideally in a payments or funding role and/or working with stablecoins</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are passionate about our mission and eager to do what needs to be done to achieve it</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are enthusiastic about treasury operations, solving unique problems, and optimizing processes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enjoy challenges, are resourceful and think outside the box to find creative ways to tackle problems</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Love working in teams and building meaningful relationships with key stakeholders</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Don’t hesitate to place a call to promptly resolve issues or persevere to get a result</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have great organisational skills and the ability to manage multiple time-sensitive priorities in a fast-paced startup environment where no two days are the same</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have proven analytical skills (Excel); SQL a plus</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are proficient in English</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Us</strong></p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re building the world’s leading cross-border fintech for emerging markets - empowering families, fuelling local economies, and changing how millions access financial services.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">Since our launch in 2019, we have transformed how money moves across borders with our operations spanning 6 out of 7 continents and covering both the busiest and most underserved  (remittance) corridors. We tapped into a massive shift - from banks to phones - bringing digital finance to places where traditional systems never reached. The next stage of growth will fuel a network of services and products especially designed to make money more accessible to diaspora communities including local cards, and additional savings and payments features.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re growing fast, backed by world-class investors, and scaling a product that blends <strong>real world impact with cutting edge fintech innovation</strong>.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">Here’s a little more:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Founded by Harvard grads and 3-time founders</strong> who previously built Segovia (acquired) and GiveDirectly (&gt;$300M revenue, fastest-growing NGO in the world)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Backed by top investors</strong> including Spark Capital, Canaan, Reid Hoffman, Breyer Capital, Unbound, Wamda, and more</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Built by global top performers</strong> from Bain, Google, McKinsey, Uber, Checkout, Bolt, and beyond - we move fast, stay humble, and care deeply about our mission</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Truly global team</strong> - 250+ people, 50+ nationalities, 50+ languages</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Guided by our values</strong> - ownership, impact, humility, and heart - in deed, not just word</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="postings-link" href="https://www.taptapsend.com/our-values"><u>Taptap Values </u></a></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Impact first</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Team next</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Accept reality</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Propose solutions</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Win with grit</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Be proactively candid, with yourself and others</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Love the particular</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own it</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create positive energy</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maybe, even have fun</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">Taptap Send is an equal opportunity employer dedicated to building an inclusive and diverse workforce. All employment decisions are decided on the basis of qualifications, experience and business need. We strongly encourage applications who are members of underrepresented communities to apply.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you require reasonable adjustments to be made during the recruitment process, please do not hesitate to let us know. Any information you provide us in this respect will only be used to accommodate your requirements.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Note: we recognize imposter syndrome is real - any candidate that does not perfectly fit every characteristic of this role is still strongly encouraged to apply.  </em></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/taptapsend/treasury-operations-analyst-london-10934","tags":["Treasury"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1792964424},{"slug":"senior-social-media-executive-london-402675","company_name":"loveholidays","title":"Senior Social Media Executive","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why loveholidays?</strong><br />At loveholidays - <strong>we trailblaze together</strong>. We’re on a mission to open the world to everyone, giving our customers’ unlimited choice, unmatched ease and unmissable value for their next getaway. Our team is the driving force behind our role as our customers’ personal holiday expert - the smart way to get away.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />We’re using progressive tech to <strong>drive cutting-edge innovation</strong> and open the world to everyone. Within our <em>Commercial and Support teams</em>, you'll find a place to <strong>accelerate your growth</strong> by actively seeking learning opportunities and carving your own path. You'll <strong>create impact for our future</strong> by owning projects and shaping the business strategy to reach shared goals, all within our <strong>enhanced international community</strong> of collaborative and passionate teams.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><strong>About the team:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll be joining our Brand Marketing team, bringing together Brand, Social, PR and Content to build awareness, strengthen trust and make loveholidays the easiest and most valuable way for customers to book their next holiday across our markets.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />We put customers at the heart of everything we do, using insight, creativity and culture to create relevant work throughout the journey, from inspiring people to dream about their next getaway to helping them book and travel with confidence. We’re a curious, collaborative team who love understanding what makes our customers tick and turning those insights into work that earns attention, adds value and supports our mission to open the world to everyone.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The impact you’ll have:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Reporting to the Senior Social Media Manager, this is an exciting opportunity to join our brand team at loveholidays, providing hands-on tactical and strategic support to build the loveholidays brand across social media channels.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />As Senior Social Media Executive, you will be instrumental in driving loveholidays’ brand engagement and visibility across various social media platforms. You will oversee the execution of our social media strategy, delivering our brand message across all live platforms with socially native, thumb stopping content. Your responsibilities will include end-to-end management and creation of social media content, managing social media platforms and communities, social listening and leveraging analytics to measure and optimise our channels for growth and content performance.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />We are looking for a creative, with strong attention to detail, a passion for social media and building brand communities online, who can hit the ground running creating content for and managing our current content calendars.<br /><br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your day-to-day:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Execute loveholidays’ social media strategy across all live platforms, bringing the brand to life through engaging, on-brand content that inspires travel and drives long-term community growth.<br /></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own and maintain the social media and marketing calendars, ensuring a consistent and timely flow of content aligned with company news, campaigns, product updates, seasonal moments and key marketing messages.<br /></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stay informed on social media trends, platform updates, emerging channels and audience behaviours, identifying opportunities to keep loveholidays’ content relevant, timely and culturally connected.<br /></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support the Senior Social Media Manager and wider content team in developing creative, community-led ideas, turning web content, customer insight and brand priorities into engaging social concepts and copy.<br /></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create high-quality, multi-format social content across video, photography, graphics, animation, written posts and interactive formats, ensuring every piece is adapted appropriately for each platform and audience.<br /></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the execution of video-first social media content, from concept development and scripting through to filming, presenting, editing and publishing, while feeling comfortable both on and off camera.<br /></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Use strong design skills to produce polished, platform-native creative, applying loveholidays’ visual identity and brand guidelines consistently across social assets, campaigns and content series.<br /></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop, test and scale repeatable content formats; manage user-generated content and influencer activity; monitor and engage with the community daily; and analyse performance data to refine strategy and report results to stakeholders.<br /></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your skillset:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong understanding of social media best practices, platform behaviours and emerging trends</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent visual judgement, with the ability to create thumb-stopping static and video content</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on content creation skills, including filming, starring-in, editing, curating and adapting content for different platforms</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven experience creating highly engaging content across Instagram, TikTok, Facebook and other relevant social channels</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to analyse social media performance data, identify actionable insights and make practical content and channel recommendations</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience using social media management, reporting and listening tools, including Sprout Social, Canva, CapCut and social listening queries<br /></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Desirable:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working across multiple markets including UK, IE, DE and SE</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience bringing brand and marketing campaigns to life through social media</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Confident using AI tools responsibly to streamline social media workflows, including ideation, planning, reporting, content repurposing and social listening, while maintaining strong editorial judgement and brand standards</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Additional language capability in German, Swedish or Polish<br /></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The interview journey:</strong></p><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Intro meet with a member of the Talent Acquisition team - 30 mins</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">1st stage with the Senior Social Media Manager - 45 mins</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Final In-office interview to present a social task with Social Media Manager &amp; a Senior stakeholder - 1 hr<br /></p></li></ol><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Perks of joining us:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Company pension contributions at 5%.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Individualised training budget for you to learn on the job and level yourself up.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Discounted holidays for you, your family and friends.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">25 days of holidays per annum (plus 8 public holidays) increases by 1 day for every second year of service, up to a maximum 30 days per annum.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to buy and sell annual leave.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cycle to work scheme, season ticket loan and eye care vouchers.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>At loveholidays, we focus on developing an inclusive culture and environment that encourages personal growth and collective success. Each individual offers unique perspectives and ideas that increase the diversity and effectiveness of our teams. And we value the insight and potential you could bring on our continued journey.</em></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/loveholidays/senior-social-media-executive-london-402675","tags"