 review electrical schematics, panel layouts, and wiring diagrams to ensure system integrity and compliance with industry standards. </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate with the team to integrate sensors, actuators, power supplies, and DAQ systems. </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Conduct system-level troubleshooting and debugging, using advanced diagnostic tools (e.g., oscilloscopes, logic analyzers, DMMs). </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Perform root cause analysis and implement engineering solutions to improve system robustness and reliability. </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Provide technical leadership during assembly, commissioning, and test operations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Document all designs, test results, and configuration changes; contribute to standard operating procedures and risk assessments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ensure all electrical systems comply with safety and regulatory standards.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><strong>Qualifications:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Minimum of a Bachelor’s degree in Electrical Engineering, Electronics, or a related technical field. </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">2+ years of experience in electrical engineering, preferably in an aerospace environment</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><strong>What we would love to see from you:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong understanding of electrical design principles, system integration, and instrumentation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with high voltage systems (200V - 1000V, AC/DC).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable working hands-on with electrical hardware, wiring, test equipment and instrumentation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven experience designing and commissioning electrical systems, and with testing of electrical systems (e.g. electrical motors and batteries)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience with cabling and harness manufacturing</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proficiency in using common electrical test equipment and CAD tools (e.g., EPLAN, AutoCAD Electrical).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with industrial control, automation or data-acquisition systems (e.g. Beckhoff).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Knowledge of electrical standards and best practices for high-reliability applications</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with test bench operations would be a plus</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable operating in a fast-paced, evolving environment with a hands-on approach. </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluency in English, both written and verbal.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A passion for space exploration and a mindset focused on innovation, precision, and safety.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why you should join us!</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">What makes us special here at The Exploration Company and why we think you will enjoy working here is:  </p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re Agile - we make decisions fast whilst keeping our goals and systems in mind </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re Open and Collaborative - we are transparent about risks and obstacles, so that we can cooperate to overcome them  </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We have a lot of Fun - we refuel our energy knowing we are democratising space. It’s a wonderful and rare opportunity, are YOU up for the challenge?  </p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">We'd love to hear from you if you wish to be a part of our journey. Please submit your CV now for immediate consideration and we will be in touch shortly. <br /> <br /><em>The Exploration Company is an equal opportunit