</li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinate with carriers, cloud connectivity providers, colocation partners, and vendors on design, provisioning, incident escalation, and service improvement.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design safe change workflows with automated validation and resilience testing, staged rollouts, observability, rollback, and recovery.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Participate in on-call rotation, troubleshoot active WAN and edge incidents, restore service, and turn root causes into lasting improvements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Review designs and code, explain networking trade-offs, and help raise network engineering quality across the organization.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>What We’re Looking For</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep, hands-on WAN and edge networking experience across internet connectivity, data-center interconnect, private WAN, or cloud networking.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record of taking external BGP designs from whiteboard to production and debugging them during production incidents.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience integrating and troubleshooting stateful firewalls, NAT, asymmetric routing, and redundant edge designs on at least one major routing or firewall platform.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building or operating production network automation using network-management APIs and data models. You understand desired state and idempotency; relevant technologies might include REST, NETCONF, gNMI/OpenConfig, Ansible, or Terraform.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong software-engineering fundamentals in a general-purpose language. You can design, test, debug, and review production systems and are willing to become productive in Go.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Operational troubleshooting experience using routing and flow state, packet captures, link health, telemetry, and logs to diagnose production incidents.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clear, pragmatic communication and effective stakeholder management. You can translate technical needs into connectivity designs and provider requirements, define acceptance criteria and service-level expectations, and provide technical leadership.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>Nice to Have</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with FortiGate, FortiManager, or comparable edge and firewall platforms.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deeper specialization in external connectivity, such as public-cloud or hybrid-cloud interconnect, or internet transit and peering.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exposure to edge security and scale techniques such as RPKI and route-origin validation, DDoS mitigation, or global traffic engineering.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with streaming telemetry, network source-of-truth systems, and configuration-compliance tooling.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience reading, reviewing, or contributing to Go code.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with Kubernetes controllers, operators, or other declarative, reconciliation-based systems.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What We Offer</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We offer a comprehensive benefits package designed to support your well-being, growth, and work-life balance. Benefits vary by country and may include healthcare coverage, parental leave, retirement plans, relocation support, wellness programs, meal and transportation allowances, and other location-specific perks.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For the most up-to-date details on benefits available in your location, please refer to our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener nore