ours.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What You Will Do</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Program Management </strong>— Oversee and manage our development and deployment processes, ensuring efficiency, effectiveness, and alignment with product timelines.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Cross-Functional Collaboration</strong> — Work closely with cross-functional teams, including Engineering, Product, Science, Marketing/Coms teams, Design, and Solutions to ensure alignment of engineering operations with overall product and business objectives.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Project Delivery</strong> — Track project progress, timelines, and resources. Assist teams to implement processes to smoothen delivery process.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Process Improvement</strong> — Continuously identify and implement process improvements to enhance the efficiency and productivity of the engineering team, in coordination with the other TPMs.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Stakeholder Management </strong>— Regularly communicate with stakeholders to provide updates on program status, risks, and issues, and to manage expectations.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Risk Management </strong>— Identify potential risks and issues in the program lifecycle, and develop contingency plans to mitigate them.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What We're Looking For</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">• You hold a degree in a relevant scientific field (e.g., Computer Science, Data Science, Engineering, etc.)<br />• You have proven experience in managing technical programs, preferably within an engineering team.<br />• You have a strong understanding of software lifecycle management and deployment processes<br />• You have excellent project management skills, with the ability to run multiple complex programs smoothly<br />• You are thriving in cross functional collaboration and