petitive benefits package.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The Sales Manager will play a key role in growing <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com">Checkout.com</a>’s payments footprint. They will be responsible for selling <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com">Checkout.com</a>’s full payments technology stack to middle market and large enterprise organizations.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Along the way, you'll collaborate closely with various in-house talents across Technology and Business to position our capabilities, products, services and solutions effectively with prospects. Desire an independent, high-achieving individual that stands out in an entrepreneurial environment and has the grit and desire to outperform sales targets.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>How you’ll make impact:</strong><br />● Acting as a consultative Payments strategist able to advise companies on an optimal payments structure that pulls from a myriad of solutions <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com">Checkout.com</a> provides<br />● Identify, qualify and close the most promising prospects and partners that will help <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com">Checkout.com</a> grow a healthy pipeline across various verticals.<br />● Build prospect engagement strategies and partner with marketing, business development, product and other departments to build qualified that pipeline in cold and warm channels<br />● Pitch our next-generation payment solutions and value-added services<br />● Prepare high-quality presentations and proposals for C-suite stakeholders at prospective merchants, and implement winning negotiation strategies<br />● Become the expert on <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com">Checkout.com</a>’s technology stack, help new merchants understand the value of <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com">Checkout.com</a> to solve their pain points, and handle detailed questions about our product capabilities.<br />● Orchestrate the entire Sales process, drive urgency and work to mutual action plans, and act as the main point of contact for merchants and internal stakeholders.<br />● Maintain a solid, well-organized portfolio and nurture key accounts by having a deep understanding of their industry, pain points, and needs.<br />● Partner with other Payment Sales Managers to share best practices, key business insights and industry trends.<br />● Provide feedback on local trends including competitor insights, customer needs, sales, product and marketing information.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Qualifications:</strong><br />● 3+ years Enterprise Sales experience ideally in the Payments industry<br />● Track record of high performance, and self sourcing leads<br />● Highly motivated and committed to growth and development with excellent communication skills<br />● Solid network of potential prospects and partners within the payments landscape<br />● Tech-savvy, with a passion for Fintech and Payments<br />● Strong commercial acumen, ability to effectively negotiate complex structures</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">● Fluent in English + French</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Additional Information</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bring all of you to work</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We create the conditions for high performers to thrive, through real ownership, fewer blockers, and work that makes a difference from day one.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Here, you’ll move fast, take on meaningful challenges, and be recognized for the impact you deliver. It’s a place where ambition gets met with opportunity, and where your growth is in your hands.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We work as one team, and we back each other to succeed. So whatever your background or identity, if you’re ready to grow and make a difference, you’ll be right at home here.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">It’s important we set you up for success and make our process as accessible as possible. So let us know in your application, or tell your recruiter directly, if you need anything to make your experience or working environment more comfortable.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Life at </strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com"><strong>Checkout.com</strong></a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We understand that work is just one part of your life. Our hybrid working model offers flexibility, with three days per week in the office to support collaboration and connection.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Curious about what it’s like to be part of our team? Visit our<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.checkout.com/careers"> <u>Careers Page</u></a> to learn more about our culture, open roles, and what drives us.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For a closer look at daily life at <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com">Checkout.com</a>, follow us on <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/checkout/life/"><u>LinkedIn</u></a> and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.instagram.com/checkout_com/"><u>Instagram</u></a></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/checkoutcom/sales-manager-paris-121299","tags":["All Departments"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Paris","created_at":1793018412},{"slug":"payroll-expert-specialist-france-paris-366173","company_name":"Backmarket","title":"Payroll Expert Specialist – France","description":"<h2>Hi, we’re Back Market.</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re here to help <strong>make tech reliable, affordable, and better than new</strong>. We're a global marketplace for refurbished devices, helping lower our collective environmental impact by providing trustworthy, affordable tech with 92% less carbon emissions than new.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Yep, you read that right. Turns out refurbished tech is way better for the planet than new. In fact, With every device purchased on Back Market, our positive impact on the planet grows. From our Customer Care representatives to our software engineer, every individual at Back Market cuts the planet — and consumers — a break. <strong>Our mission is simple: to do more with what we already have.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are you ready to join us?</p><h1><strong>Are you ready to join us?</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our People team is on a mission to make work life smoother for every Back Maker — and payroll is at the heart of it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re in the middle of an exciting HR transformation: strengthening our in-house payroll expertise, automating People Operations, and improving the employee experience through smarter processes and tools.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Based in Paris or Bordeaux, you’ll join our Payroll &amp; People Operations team and take ownership of French payroll for approximately 300 employees (523 in France), with a scope that will continue to grow. You’ll also contribute to our international payroll operations and HR automation roadmap, leveraging Workday and AI-powered tools to make our processes more efficient, reliable, and scalable.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Reporting to the Lead Payroll &amp; People Operations, you’ll combine hands-on payroll expertise, and end to end payroll cycle in house , close collaboration with external providers (international), and a continuous improvement mindset.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>YOUR MISSION (IF YOU ACCEPT IT): 🏅</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own and manage French payroll</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the end-to-end French payroll process, ensuring accurate and timely salary payments for approximately 300 employees in house payroll.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collect and verify payroll inputs, review payslips, perform reconciliations, and ensure the accuracy of taxes, social security contributions, and other payroll-related payments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage employee lifecycle changes, from onboarding to offboarding, ensuring all payroll-related information and documentation are accurate and up to date in SIRH</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Handle recurring legal and social declarations, including DSN submissions and year-end declarations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Monitor changes in French payroll regulations and employment legislation, working closely with our Legal team to ensure compliance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain accurate payroll records, documentation, and reporting to support audits and ensure reliable processes.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work closely with external payroll and benefits providers, as well as local administrations when needed, to ensure smooth and compliant operations.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Drive People Operations and payroll automation</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute to the implementation and optimisation of Workday, our HR core system, to automate People Operations workflows and payroll preparation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Explore opportunities to leverage AI and automation to streamline payroll processes, reduce manual tasks, and improve data accuracy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify opportunities to improve existing processes, documentation, and benefits administration, including health insurance and lunch card registrations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help build scalable, efficient, and well-documented processes as our organisation continues to grow.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Provide a great employee experience</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Respond to employees’ payroll and People Operations questions in a timely, clear, and approachable manner.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Investigate and resolve payroll discrepancies and employee issues with care and attention to detail.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Communicate payroll-related changes proactively, ensuring employees feel informed and supported.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>YOU ARE IN THE RIGHT PLACE IF ⭐</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You have:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">4-6+ years of hands-on experience processing French payroll, with a strong understanding of French social security, tax requirements, and employment legislation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience managing end-to-end payroll operations, including payroll inputs, payslip checks, reconciliations, and social declarations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working with external payroll providers and coordinating with multiple stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong analytical skills, excellent organisational skills, and exceptional attention to detail.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluency in both French and English, enabling you to communicate effectively in an international environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A structured, autonomous, and proactive approach, with a strong sens