es worldwide.</p><p>Today, SkyCell operates at the intersection of hardware, software, data, and logistics - combining Swiss engineering excellence with a growing digital platform to shape the future of connected pharma supply chains.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>Why SkyCell?</strong></p><p>🌱 Purpose-Driven Work: Make a real difference by contributing to a more sustainable future in global logistics and healthcare.</p><p>🚀 Innovation at Heart: Work with cutting-edge technology and be at the forefront of supply chain innovation.</p><p>🌎 Stronger together: Join a supportive team of talented individuals from over 40 countries, where we work together every step of the way.</p><p>💡 Growth Opportunities: We believe in investing in our people – continuous learning and development are key pillars of SkyCell.</p><p>🏆 Award-Winning Culture: Join a workplace recognized for its commitment to excellence with a ‘Great Place to work’ award, as well as a Platinum Ecovadis rating highlighting our sustainability and employee well-being.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>What You'll Do:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Design and implement embedded firmware for low-power IoT devices using C/C++ (RTOS or bare-metal)</p></li><li><p>Integrate wireless communication technologies such as BLE, LoRa or Cellular</p></li><li><p>Design, build and operate cloud-side ingestion pipelines and device fleet management systems for large-scale IoT deployments</p></li><li><p>Contribute to the design and deployment of cloud architectures for IoT integrations</p></li><li><p>Implement secure and reliable OTA update mechanisms for remote firmware management</p></li><li><p>Build and maintain CI/CD pipelines for firmware and cloud components (e.g. GitHub Actions)</p></li><li><p>Collaborate with colleagues across firmware, hardware and cloud teams</p></li><li><p>Troubleshoot complex system-level issues across device, connectivity and cloud layers</p></li><li><p>Contribute to architecture