Engineer - Expenses Team","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Join BLP and help make the world’s business processes autonomous! </strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our agentic platform helps finance and operations teams worldwide remove manual work from their core business processes, so work runs end-to-end with greater control and significant productivity gains. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Today, over 550 enterprise customers use BLP across 1,300+ deployed projects. In the processes we automate, customers achieve productivity improvements of 5 to 10 times. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">To date, BLP remains majority employee-owned, with Goldman Sachs holding a minority stake as a growth investor. Our success is driven by deep expertise in technology and business processes, a superior product with strong product-market fit, reflected in an expanding customer base that includes Fortune 500 companies. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">BLP is one of Switzerland's fastest-growing SaaS scale-ups; we are now entering our next phase of growth. From our headquarters on Zürich's Bahnhofstrasse, we're expanding globally, with a growing presence across Europe and North America. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Join us and help make autonomous operations the new standard. </em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>About the role</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>End-to-end expense automation: </strong>You’d work on a web app, and the BLP company card, where receipts are captured, read by AI (OCR and agents), matched to card transactions, and posted to the customer’s ERP with minimal manual effort.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>ERP integrations and card infrastructure:</strong> We’re building interfaces to systems such as SAP, F&amp;O, and proAlpha, along with multi-currency, fee, and tip booking logic and card transaction processing via our card partner.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Market expansion:</strong> We’re rolling out in Switzerland from early 2027 and in Germany from Q3 2027, which means new capabilities such as per diem allowances and kilometer expenses.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What’s next:</strong> Travel management integrations are planned for 2027, with automatic expense creation from bookings, handling of trip changes and cancellations, and consolidated travel reporting.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2>What you'll do</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Drive Impact:</strong> Collaborate with business stakeholders to understand requirements and translate them into possible improvements to our product.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build Great Software:</strong> Design and develop clean, maintainable, and high-quality software, applying a wide range of principles including functional patterns. Conduct code reviews and contribute to a culture of technical excellence. </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Lead and Influence:</strong> Guide technical direction for major initiatives, shape how the product evolves and mentor team members along the way.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Promote Innovation and Collaboration:</strong> Work closely with colleagues, share what you learn openly, and continuously improve processes, tools, and team practices.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The Tech Stack for this role includes Golang, MySQL, Docker images deployed on a Kubernetes cluster in our cloud infrastructure (GCS, AWS or Azure) and Github CI/CD. </p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2>What you'll bring</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bachelor's or Master's degree in Computer Science or equivalent practical experience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">3+ years of experience in a software engineering role.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Passionate about software craftsmanship: Strong understanding of software development principles, Clean Code and Clean Architecture.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Product thinking: Ability to translate business problems into precise requirements, specifications and ultimately into code.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Entrepreneurial mindset: link your daily work to team and company goals, balance cost and benefit, deliver high-quality solutions efficiently.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ownership: take responsibility for your technical work, for the product we build and the team we shape.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Team-oriented: proactively support team goals, close gaps.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Abstraction and efficient communication: simplify complex systems, identify core concepts, communicate complex ideas to different stakeholders. </p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2>What you'll get</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Full ownership.</strong> You own the product's roadmap, from business problem to shipped code.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>End-to-end impact.</strong> You're on a team that owns what it builds, start to finish.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A modern, varied tech stack.</strong> Continuous learning as the platform scales.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">Learn more about blp and our values at <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://blp.digital/company/careers">blp.digital/company/careers</a>.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/blp-digital-ag/software-engineer-expenses-team-zurich-72683","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Zurich","created_at":1792669233},{"slug":"strategic-account-executive-switzerland-376413","company_name":"ElevenLabs","title":"Strategic Account Executive - Switzerland","description":"<h2>About ElevenLabs</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">ElevenLabs is an AI research and product company transforming how we interact with technology.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We launched in January 2023 with the first human-like AI voice model. Today, we serve millions of users and thousands of businesses - from fast-growing startups to large enterprises like Deutsche Telekom and Meta. Our investors are some of the world's most prominent, including Andreessen Horowitz, ICONIQ Growth and Sequoia. We've raised $781M in funding and our last valuation was $22B - multiples of 11, always.<br /><br />We have expanded from voice into three main platforms:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">ElevenAgents enables businesses to deliver seamless and intelligent customer experiences, with the integrations, testing, monitoring, and reliability necessary to deploy voice and chat agents at scale.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">ElevenCreative empowers creators and marketers to generate and edit speech, music, image, and video across 70+ languages.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">ElevenAPI gives developers access to our leading AI audio foundational models.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Everything we do is the result of the creativity and commitment of our team - builders doing the best work of their lives. We are researchers, engineers, and operators. IOI medalists and ex-founders. If you want to work hard and create lasting positive impact, we want to hear from you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>How we work</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>High-velocity: </strong>Rapid experimentation, lean autonomous teams, and minimal bureaucracy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Impact not job titles: </strong>We don’t have job titles. Instead, it’s about the impact you have. No task is above or beneath you.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI first:</strong> We use AI to move faster with higher-quality results. We do this across the whole company—from engineering to growth to operations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Excellence everywhere: </strong>Everything we do should match the quality of our AI models.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Global team: </strong>We prioritize your talent, not your location.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What we offer</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Innovative culture:</strong> You’ll be part of a generational opportunity to define the trajectory of AI, surrounded by a team pushing the boundaries of what’s possible.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Growth paths: </strong>Joining ElevenLabs means joining a dynamic team with countless opportunities to drive impact - beyond your immediate role and responsibilities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Learning &amp; development</strong>: ElevenLabs proactively supports professional development through an annual discretionary stipend.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Social travel</strong>: We also provide an annual discretionary stipend to meet up with colleagues each year, however you choose.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Annual company offsite: </strong>Each year, we bring the entire team together in a new location - past offsites have included Croatia and Italy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Co-working</strong>: If you’re not located near one of our main hubs, we offer a monthly co-working stipend.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for an experienced, driven Strategic Account Executive to drive ElevenLabs' growth across Switzerland's largest enterprises. Our ideal candidate has a well-established network and a proven track record of selling to C-level and senior decision-makers at major Swiss brands and is passionate about the transformative possibilities of AI voice technology.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">In this role you'll act as a strategic partner and trusted advisor, enabling clients to leverage our industry-leading models and ElevenAgents — our end-to-end platform for building and deploying AI voice agents — to reimagine their customer experience, internal workflows, and monetization strategies.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">In this role you will:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and manage a growing portfolio of strategic accounts across Switzerland to help ElevenLabs meet its revenue goals.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify new business opportunities where ElevenLabs' conversational AI capabilities, including ElevenAgents, can drive customer engagement, contact center automation, and operational efficiency for consumer and retail brands.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead consultative, multi-stakeholder sales cycles, building compelling business cases that translate AI voice technology into measurable business value for senior executives and economic buyers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop and maintain a deep understanding of the conversational AI landscape, including customer use cases, competitive solutions, and emerging trends, particularly as they apply to Swiss consumer and retail organizations operating at scale.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demonstrate expertise, or a strong willingness to learn, about conversational AI and how ElevenLabs' voice technology can unlock value across customer support, virtual agents, IVR modernization, and in-app assistants.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop and execute account strategies to expand ElevenLabs' presence within the Swiss consumer and retail sector, navigating complex procurement and organizational structures.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner closely with Customer Success, FDEs and Solutions Engineering to ensure smooth onboarding, deployment, and expansion of accounts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Serve as a trusted advisor to clients, educating C-suite and senior operations leaders on emerging trends in generative AI, voice interfaces, and conversational agents.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Requirements</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">7+ years of quota-carrying strategic sales experience in SaaS or technology, ideally with exposure to AI, generative AI, LLM-based products, or API-driven platforms.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven success closing deals and managing long, complex sales cycles with multiple stakeholders across business, IT, legal, and procurement.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Well-connected in the Swiss consumer and retail landscape, with an existing network of senior individuals and strong executive presence and ability to build relationships at the C-suite and board level.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience selling technical solutions to product and engineering leaders; ability to translate complex technology into business value.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep understanding of enterprise procurement and legal processes in Switzerland, with the ability to accelerate deal velocity within complex organizational structures.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort operating in an early-stage, high-growth environment, including building new playbooks and iterating quickly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Passion for voice and audio AI and how it can unlock transformative value for customers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A hybrid of customer and product-driven mentality that prioritizes client satisfaction and scale.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Swiss German is the preferred default language for this role; fluency in both Swiss German and French is a strong plus given Switzerland's multilingual market. Strong English is also required for internal collaboration.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Location</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is an in-country role based in Zurich.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are an equal opportunity employer and do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, veteran status, disability or other legally protected statuses.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are an equal opportunity employer and do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, veteran status, disability or other legally protected statuses.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/elevenlabs/strategic-account-executive-switzerland-376413","tags":["Revenue"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Switzerland","created_at":1792669229},{"slug":"gestionnaire-ressources-humaines-geneva-142613","company_name":"Beau-Rivage Genève","title":"Gestionnaire Ressources Humaines","description":"<h2>L’humain au cœur de la Maison, contribuez à faire vivre l’expérience Beau-Rivage de l’intérieur.</h2><br><br>Niché au cœur de Genève, notre palace emblématique incarne l’élégance, le raffinement et l’excellence du service hôtelier de luxe. Engagé dans un ambitieux projet de rénovation visant à sublimer son héritage tout en redéfinissant les standards contemporains du luxe, l’établissement ouvre un nouveau chapitre de son histoire.<br><br>Pour accompagner cette transformation et soutenir nos équipes au quotidien, nous recherchons notre futur(e) <strong>Gestionnaire Ressources Humaines H/F</strong>.<br><br>Votre mission :<br><br>Rattaché(e) à la Directrice des Ressources Humaines, vous assurez la gestion RH quotidienne et accompagnez les collaborateurs tout au long de leur parcours au sein de la Maison.<br><br>Véritable interlocuteur(trice) de proximité, vous intervenez sur l’ensemble des sujets liés à l’administration du personnel, à la paie, au recrutement et à l’expérience collaborateur.<br><br>Polyvalent(e), autonome et organisé(e), vous évoluez au sein d’une équipe RH à taille humaine et contribuez activement à garantir une gestion fiable et rigoureuse, tout en maintenant une relation de proximité avec les collaborateurs et les équipes opérationnelles.<br><br>Vos responsabilités principales :<br><br><ul><li><strong>Administration du personnel :</strong> Assurer la gestion administrative des collaborateurs, de leur entrée à leur sortie : contrats, avenants, attestations, certificats de travail, permis de travail et autres documents RH.</li><li><strong>Suivi des collaborateurs :</strong> Garantir la bonne tenue des dossiers collaborateurs, la fiabilité des données administratives et leur mise à jour régulière.</li><li><strong>Gestion des absences :</strong> Assurer le suivi des absences, vacances, congés et certificats médicaux.</li><li><strong>Accompagnement RH :</strong> Être un point de contact privilégié pour les collaborateurs et répondre à leurs questions relatives aux différents sujets RH.</li><li><strong>Onboarding & Offboarding :</strong> Coordonner les différentes étapes d’intégration et de départ des collaborateurs, en collaboration avec la Direction des Ressources Humaines et les départements concernés.</li><li><strong>Paie & Gestion des temps :</strong> Assurer le processus mensuel des salaires, le suivi des temps de travail et des éléments variables de paie jusqu’à la clôture.</li><li><strong>Recrutement :</strong> Participer à l’ensemble du processus de recrutement selon les besoins : publication des annonces, suivi des candidatures, entretiens et accompagnement jusqu’à l’engagement définitif.</li><li><strong>Relations Écoles :</strong> Contribuer au développement et au suivi des partenariats avec les écoles hôtelières afin de renforcer notre attractivité auprès des futurs talents.</li><li><strong>Communication & Événements internes :</strong> Participer à la communication RH ainsi qu’à l’organisation des événements destinés aux collaborateurs.</li><li><strong>Projets RH & Expérience Collaborateur :</strong> Contribuer aux différents projets RH et proposer des initiatives visant à améliorer continuellement l’expérience collaborateur.</li></ul><br><br>Profil :<br><br><ul><li><strong>Formation :</strong> Vous êtes diplômé(e) d’une <strong>école hôtelière (Bachelor ou équivalent)</strong> et avez complété votre parcours par une <strong>formation en Ressources Humaines</strong>.</li><li><strong>Expérience :</strong> Vous disposez d’une expérience d’au minimum <strong>3 ans dans une fonction RH similaire</strong>, obligatoirement acquise dans le secteur de <strong>l’hôtellerie-restauration</strong>.</li><li><strong>Paie :</strong> Vous maîtrisez les processus de paie, le suivi des temps de travail et la gestion des éléments variables de salaire.</li><li><strong>Connaissances RH :</strong> Vous disposez idéalement de bonnes connaissances du <strong>droit du travail suisse et des assurances sociales</strong>.</li><li><strong>Outils :</strong> Vous êtes à l’aise avec les outils informatiques et les systèmes d’information RH.</li><li><strong>Organisation :</strong> Rigoureux(se) et organisé(e), vous savez gérer plusieurs priorités simultanément et assurer un suivi précis de vos dossiers.</li><li><strong>Relationnel :</strong> Vous appréciez le contact humain et savez instaurer une relation de confiance avec vos interlocuteurs, tout en respectant la stricte confidentialité inhérente à la fonction RH.</li><li><strong>Posture :</strong> Autonome, dynamique et polyvalent(e), vous appréciez de travailler au sein d’une petite équipe où l’entraide, la réactivité et l’autonomie sont essentielles.</li><li><strong>Langues :</strong> Vous maîtrisez parfaitement le <strong>français, à l’oral comme à l’écrit</strong>. La maîtrise de l’anglais constitue un réel atout.</li><li><strong>Personnalité :</strong> Vous êtes force de proposition, orienté(e) solutions et aimez contribuer à une ambiance de travail positive.</li></ul><br><br>Pourquoi rejoindre la Maison Beau-Rivage ?<br><br><ul><li>Une fonction RH <strong>polyvalente et proche du terrain</strong>, au cœur de la vie de la Maison.</li><li>L’opportunité d’accompagner les collaborateurs à chaque étape de leur parcours.</li><li>Une participation active à la transformation d’un établissement emblématique en pleine rénovation.</li><li>Des missions variées associant <strong>administration RH, paie, recrutement, relations écoles et expérience collaborateur</strong>.</li><li>Un environnement de travail stimulant et exigeant au cœur de Genève.</li><li>La possibilité de contribuer concrètement aux projets RH qui accompagneront le nouveau chapitre de Beau-Rivage.</li></ul><br><br><h2><strong>Rejoignez Beau-Rivage et contribuez à faire vivre une expérience collaborateur à la hauteur de l’excellence de notre Maison. </strong></h2><h2></h2><br><br>Nos offres d’emploi s’adressent autant aux femmes qu’aux hommes.<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/beau-rivage-geneve/gestionnaire-ressources-humaines-geneva-142613","tags":["HR"],"job_types":["professionnel / expérimenté"],"location":"Geneva","created_at":1792668689},{"slug":"werkstudentin-implementation-customer-operations-zurich-317935","company_name":"Selise Group AG","title":"Werkstudent*in (m/w/d) Implementation & Customer Operations","description":"<p><strong>ORDERMONKEY by SELISE | Zürich | Teilzeit (40+ %) Start: Ab Q1 2027</strong></p><h3>Du interessierst dich für Technologie, Digitalisierung und Gastronomie?</h3><p>Du möchtest neben deinem Studium praktische Erfahrungen in einem innovativen Tech-Unternehmen sammeln und aktiv an der Digitalisierung der Gastronomie mitarbeiten?</p><p>Dann bist du bei <strong>ORDERMONKEY</strong> genau richtig!</p><p>ORDERMONKEY ist eine innovative Self-Ordering-Plattform der internationalen Technologie- und Softwareentwicklungsfirma <strong>SELISE</strong>. Mit unseren digitalen Lösungen – von Self-Ordering-Kiosks über Webshops bis hin zu Payment- und Loyalty-Systemen – unterstützen wir führende Gastronomieunternehmen dabei, ihre Prozesse effizienter und das Kundenerlebnis besser zu gestalten.</p><p>Für unser Team suchen wir eine motivierte, selbstständige Persönlichkeit, die uns im operativen Tagesgeschäft, bei Kundenprojekten und bei der Einführung unserer Lösungen unterstützt.</p><h2>Deine Aufgaben</h2><p>Als Werkstudent bist du Teil unseres Operations-Teams und unterstützt uns bei der Umsetzung spannender Digitalisierungsprojekte.</p><ul><li><p><strong>Projektkoordination:</strong> Du unterstützt bei der Planung, Vorbereitung und Umsetzung von Kundenprojekten.</p></li><li><p><strong>Kunden-Onboarding:</strong> Du hilfst neuen Kunden beim Einstieg in unsere Plattform und bei der Einrichtung ihrer digitalen Lösungen.</p></li><li><p><strong>Installation & Rollout:</strong> Du unterstützt bei der Vorbereitung, Koordination und gelegentlich bei der Installation unserer Self-Ordering-Kiosks vor Ort.</p></li><li><p><strong>Testing & Qualitätssicherung:</strong> Du testest neue Funktionen und arbeitest mit unserem internationalen Produkt- und Entwicklungsteam zusammen.</p></li><li><p><strong>Customer Success:</strong> Du unterstützt unsere Kunden bei Fragen und hilfst dabei, einfache technische Herausforderungen zu lösen.</p></li><li><p><strong>Prozessoptimierung: