t is: you monitor pipeline health, check the quality of predictions, optimizations and simulations, investigate anomalies and turn recurring manual checks into reliable tooling. You work closely with our ML engineers and Customer Success, and you see directly how your work shapes our customers' budget decisions.</p><h2>Your responsibilities</h2><h3>Monitor the automation and assure result quality</h3><ul><li><p>Monitor the automated prediction, optimization and simulation pipelines across customer portfolios and track run health, completeness and timeliness.</p></li><li><p>Verify that predictions, optimization proposals and simulation results meet our quality standards before they reach customers: budget shifts, expected KPI changes, channel constraints and funnel-level effects.</p></li><li><p>Investigate failed or unexpected runs, identify the root cause (data, configuration or model) and resolve it or escalate it with a clear diagnosis.</p></li></ul><h3>Assure the quality of results over time</h3><ul><li><p>Define and maintain plausibility checks for optimization and simulation results, for example for budget planning, seasonal shifts or new channel tests.</p></li><li><p>Make sure results are consistent and explainable, so that customers and account managers can trust them without manual checks.</p></li><li><p>Compare optimized and simulated outcomes with realized performance, document deviations and feed the findings back to the ML team.</p></li></ul><h3>Safeguard data and model quality</h3><ul><li><p>Monitor input data for gaps, anomalies and tracking changes that affect optimization quality.</p></li><li><p>Track model fit and prediction accuracy per portfolio and flag degradation early.</p></li><li><p>Maintain portfolio configurations such as funnel steps, constraints and target definitions together with the responsible teams.</p></li></ul><h3>Automate the operational workflow</h3><ul><li><p>Replace manual checks with Python scripts, validation rules and alerts.</p></li><li><p>Build and maintain dashboards that show run status, data health and model performance across portfolios.</p></li><li><p>Write runbooks so that operational knowledge is shared, not held by one person.</p></li></ul><h2>The impact you will have</h2><ul><li><p>Customers receive optimization proposals and simulations that are correct and delivered on time.</p></li><li><p>Issues are caught before customers see them, not after.</p></li><li><p>The time the ML team spends on operational work goes down measurably, because recurring steps are automated.</p></li><li><p>Customer Success can trust automated optimization and simulation results without checking them by hand.</p></li></ul><h2>Your experience and skills</h2><ul><li><p>Recently completed Master's degree in Data Science, Computer Science, Statistics, Mathematics, Engineering or a related field.</p></li><li><p>Solid Python skills, including pandas and NumPy, and comfort working with SQL.</p></li><li><p>Good understanding of statistics and basic machine learning concepts such as regression, model evaluation and overfitting.</p></li><li><p>A careful, structured way of working: you check results before you share them and you document what you do.</p></li><li><p>Ability to explain technical findings clearly to non-technical colleagues.</p></li><li><p>Fluent English, spoken and written, is a must.</p></li></ul><h2>Bonus points</h2><ul><li><p>Experience with optimization methods, for example constrained or non-convex optimization.</p></li><li><p>Familiarity with Marketing Mix Modeling, attribution or digital advertising metrics.</p></li><li><p>Experience with data pipelines, scheduled jobs or monitoring tools.</p></li><li><p>Experience with Git, Docker and cloud environments.</p></li><li><p>Fluent in German or Italian.</p></li></ul><h2>Your future work life</h2><ul><li><p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Your work directly influences how enterprise marketers allocate their budgets.</p></li><li><p><strong>Responsibility:</strong> You own the quality of a defined part of our automation from day one, with a personal development roadmap and regular feedback.</p></li><li><p><strong>Learning:</strong> You work alongside experienced ML and data engineers on production systems, not on side projects.</p></li><li><p><strong>Culture:</strong> A transparent company culture at eye level, where every person is valued and supported.</p></li><li><p><strong>Strategy:</strong> You take part in shaping company strategy and culture during our quarterly Strategy Days.</p></li><li><p><strong>Events:</strong> Regular team events, on-site and off-site.</p></li></ul><h2>Application process</h2><ul><li><p>Profile review and short phone screen</p></li><li><p>Take-home case study</p></li><li><p>Case discussion with the ML team</p></li><li><p>On-site interview and team evaluation</p></li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/nexoya/ml-intern-optimization-quality-monitoring-zurich-167634","tags":["Quality Assurance","Inspection"],"job_types":["Internship (praktikumsvertrag)","internship","entry"],"location":"Zürich","created_at":1792663256},{"slug":"digital-marketing-retail-zurich-463647","company_name":"Homberger Personalberatung für Kommunikation","title":"Digital Marketing Retail","description":"<p>Im Auftrag unseres Kunden suchen wir eine erfahrene, kreative und umsetzungsstarke Persönlichkeit im</p><h2>Digital Marketing Retail (60%)</h2><p>An der Schnittstelle von Fashion, Retail, Gestaltung und Digital Marketing erwartet Sie eine vielseitige Rolle:</p><ul><li>Verantwortung für die Planung und Umsetzung sämtlicher Marketingmassnahmen</li><li>Umsetzung der Marketingstrategie</li><li>Gestaltung von Werbemitteln wie Plakate, Flyer, Einladungen und POS-Materialien</li><li>Aufbereitung und Koordination von Marketingmaterialien</li><li>Umsetzung von Ma