 Manager, SEMrush, Ahrefs, or similar tools</strong>.</li><li>Experience managing <strong>Google Ads and paid social media campaigns</strong>.</li><li>Familiarity with WordPress, Webflow, or other CMS platforms.</li><li>Understanding of conversion rate optimization (CRO), landing pages, and lead generation funnels.</li><li>Experience with CRM and marketing automation platforms.</li><li>Strong analytical skills and ability to translate data into actionable improvements.</li><li>Excellent written and verbal English communication skills.</li><li>Ability to independently manage multiple campaigns and meet deadlines.</li><li>Availability during <strong>U.S. Business Hours</strong>.</li></ul><h2><strong>Preferred Qualifications</strong></h2><ul><li>Experience with <strong>Answer Engine Optimization (AEO)</strong> and <strong>Generative Engine Optimization (GEO)</strong>.</li><li>Knowledge of local SEO and Google Business Profile optimization.</li><li>Familiarity with HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and technical website improvements.</li><li>Experience in B2B marketing, SaaS, professional services, or lead-generation businesses.</li><li>Experience with Looker Studio and advanced marketing reporting.</li><li>Certifications in Google Ads, Google Analytics, HubSpot, or SEO.</li></ul><h2><strong>What Makes You a Strong Fit</strong></h2><ul><li>You take ownership of marketing performance and focus on measurable results.</li><li>You understand how SEO, paid advertising, content, and conversion optimization work together.</li><li>You can independently develop strategies, execute campaigns, and analyze performance.</li><li>You’re proactive about identifying growth opportunities and testing improvements.</li><li>You stay informed about search engine updates and emerging AI-powered marketing trends.</li><li>You communicate clearly and collaborate effectively with remote teams.</li></ul><h2><strong>What a Typical Day Looks Like</strong></h2><p>Your day may begin by reviewing <strong>GA4, Goo